liams, Jessica (1989- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': '2 Dope Queens (Radio Program)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-01T10:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af5f5dc7-c52d-581f-b70c-91d92c67da94', 'word_count': 1159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af5f5dc7-c52d-581f-b70c-91d92c67da94'}, {'abstract': 'Normally a workhorse, he began feeling strangely exhausted. Then he ended up in the intensive-care unit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/01/magazine/tests-indicated-his-infection-was-getting-better-why-did-he-feel-worse.html', 'snippet': 'Normally a workhorse, he began feeling strangely exhausted. Then he ended up in the intensive-care unit.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Something’s wrong,” the woman told the young doctor, her face lined with worry. “This is not my husband.” The 68-year-old man lay unmoving in the hospital bed, his eyes dull, his face expressionless. His wife stood by him, as she had for nearly four decades of marriage. You don’t know him, she said, but if you did, you’d know that something is not right.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/04/magazine/04mag-diagnosis1/04mag-04diagnosis-t_CA0-articleLarge.png', 'height': 554, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/04/magazine/04mag-diagnosis1/04mag-04diagnosis-t_CA0-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 554}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/04/magazine/04mag-diagnosis1/04mag-04diagnosis-t_CA0-jumbo.png', 'height': 945, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/04/magazine/04mag-diagnosis1/04mag-04diagnosis-t_CA0-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1890, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/04/magazine/04mag-diagnosis1/04mag-04diagnosis-t_CA0-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/04/magazine/04mag-diagnosis1/04mag-04diagnosis-t_CA0-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/04/magazine/04mag-diagnosis1/04mag-04diagnosis-t_CA0-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tests Indicated His Infection Was Getting Better. Why Did He Feel Worse?', 'kicker': 'Diagnosis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After the man was treated for a bad infection, tests indicated he was getting better. So why was he feeling weaker by the day?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bacteria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-01T10:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Sanders, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sanders', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0853b12e-49aa-532f-a7c6-e871e62de66d', 'word_count': 1407, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0853b12e-49aa-532f-a7c6-e871e62de66d'}, {'abstract': 'By studying the natural effects of a large volcanic eruption, scientists could learn about how we might deliberately cool the planet in the future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/01/climate/volcano-geoengineering.html', 'snippet': 'By studying the natural effects of a large volcanic eruption, scientists could learn about how we might deliberately cool the planet in the future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A quarter-century ago, Pinatubo, a volcano in the Philippines, blew its top in a big way: It spewed a cubic mile of rock and ash and 20 million tons of sulfur dioxide gas into the atmosphere. The gas spread around the world and combined with water vapor to make aerosols, tiny droplets that reflected some sunlight away from the Earth. As a result, average global temperatures dropped by about one degree Fahrenheit for several years.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/29/climate/29cli-volcanoes/29cli-volcanoes-articleLarge-v5.gif', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/29/climate/29cli-volcanoes/29cli-volcanoes-articleLarge-v5.gif', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/29/climate/29cli-volcanoes/29cli-volcanoes-jumbo-v3.gif', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/29/climate/29cli-volcanoes/29cli-volcanoes-superJumbo-v4.gif', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_na