ne, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-02-01T12:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NewsDesk', 'section_name': 'Briefing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Des Shoe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Des', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shoe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/182001d6-e5f9-5689-92d8-db2f6f64618e', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/182001d6-e5f9-5689-92d8-db2f6f64618e'}, {'abstract': 'Slowing down from its dance music mode, the group Above & Beyond chills out on conventional instruments in this documentary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/01/movies/above-and-beyond-acoustic-giving-up-the-day-job-review.html', 'snippet': 'Slowing down from its dance music mode, the group Above & Beyond chills out on conventional instruments in this documentary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The trio Above & Beyond originated as an electronic dance music group, and became popular in that iteration. In 2014 the group made an album called “Acoustic,” which featured them playing conventional instruments rather than samplers and decks. In this film, the group tours in support of that and similar work with a large retinue of singers and instrumentalists, culminating in a gig at the Hollywood Bowl.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/02/movies/02above1/merlin_132730760_7684b0da-13fa-4c61-8d5c-982c7e8a5db3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/02/movies/02above1/merlin_132730760_7684b0da-13fa-4c61-8d5c-982c7e8a5db3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'imag