_id': 'nyt://article/030f34ce-d8cc-5452-a31e-2b6264892fcc', 'word_count': 1643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/030f34ce-d8cc-5452-a31e-2b6264892fcc'}, {'abstract': 'Hear how the pianist created his definitive, career-making 1955 recording of Bach’s “Goldberg” Variations — one misstep at a time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/02/arts/music/glenn-gould-bach-goldberg-variations.html', 'snippet': 'Hear how the pianist created his definitive, career-making 1955 recording of Bach’s “Goldberg” Variations — one misstep at a time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sitting comfortably in my living room, I had every intention of listening to the boxed set that had recently landed with a thud in my mailbox. For Bach lovers, Glenn Gould fans and pianists (I’m all three), here was  perhaps the ultimate find of recording history, finally available: the nearly five hours of Gould’s complete recording sessions for his momentous debut album, Bach’s “Goldberg” Variations.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/04/arts/04GOULD-extra/04GOULD-extra-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 414, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/04/arts/04GOULD-extra/04GOULD-extra-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 414}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/04/arts/04GOULD-extra/04GOULD-extra-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 706, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/04/arts/04GOULD-extra/04GOULD-extra-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1221, 'width': 1771, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 't