r the leeward side of the boat, facing downwind. Don’t feel ashamed. For Kwachka, it helps to keep the mood light. He tells the crew he’s going to “look for Buicks,” vomits over the side and then sneezes. “That seems to reset things,” he says.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/04/magazine/04mag-tip/04mag-04tip-t_CA0-articleLarge.png', 'height': 672, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/04/magazine/04mag-tip/04mag-04tip-t_CA0-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 672}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/04/magazine/04mag-tip/04mag-04tip-t_CA0-jumbo.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 915, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/04/magazine/04mag-tip/04mag-04tip-t_CA0-superJumbo.png', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1829, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/04/magazine/04mag-tip/04mag-04tip-t_CA0-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/04/magazine/04mag-tip/04mag-04tip-t_CA0-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/04/magazine/04mag-tip/04mag-04tip-t_CA0-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Overcome Seasickness', 'kicker': 'Tip', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 