slideshow/dbca0714-f90d-5a42-834e-2c66193ea016'}, {'abstract': 'The eyes of the world will be on Pyeongchang in a week. Andrew Keh arrived Friday. Here is what he saw.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/02/sports/what-is-pyeongchang.html', 'snippet': 'The eyes of the world will be on Pyeongchang in a week. Andrew Keh arrived Friday. Here is what he saw.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GANGNEUNG, South Korea — Early Friday morning, in a hallway outside the Olympic media dining room, a young woman stocked a long row of shelves with Korean novels translated into a dozen or so languages. The books were free to take or borrow, she said. The Pyeongchang Organizing Committee for the Olympic Games hoped to introduce international visitors to Korean literature and other aspects of the national culture.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/03/sports/03pyeongchang1/03pyeongchang1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/03/sports/03pyeongchang1/03pyeongchang1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/03/sports/03pyeongchang1/03pyeongchang1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/03/sports/03pyeongchang1/03pyeongchang1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/03/sports/03pyeongchang1/03pyeongchang1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/03/sports/03pyeongchang1/03pyeongchang1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/03/sports/03pyeongchang1/03pyeongchang1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Sportswriter’s First Impressions of Pyeongchang', 'kicker': 'On Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pyeongchang: Warm Welcome In the Icy Cold', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2018)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pyeongchang (South Korea)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-02T16:45:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46245cd1-cefb-53f2-a64c-c964517f4fae', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46245cd1-cefb-53f2-a64c-c964517f4fae'}, {'abstract': 'Proposals to include a cavernous, tiger-shaped underground studio and a 40-foot tower were rejected by preservation authorities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/02/arts/design/munch-house-to-die.html', 'snippet': 'Proposals to include a cavernous, tiger-shaped underground studio and a 40-foot tower were rejected by preservation authorities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OSLO — For the last 28 years of his life, the artist Edvard Munch lived in a villa in a hilly, forested area that was then on the outskirts of this city. He completed hundreds of paintings and drawings there, and the estate,  Ekely, has become a pilgrimage site for fans of his art. Although Munch’s villa was demolished in 1960, and an artists’ colony now exists on the site, his enclosed winter studio remains, and visitors can walk among the nearby trees to discover the surroundings that inspired many of his later works.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/03/arts/03OSLO4/03OSLO4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 436, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/03/arts/03OSLO4/03OSLO4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 436}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/03/arts/03OSLO4/03OSLO4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/03/arts/03OSLO4/03OSLO4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1489, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/03/arts/03OSLO4/03OSLO4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/03/arts/03OSLO4/03OSLO4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/03/arts/03OSLO4/03OSLO4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Artist Wants to Build a U.F.O. Next to Edvard Munch’s Studio', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.F.O. Hovers Over Sacred Terrain', 'n