ival.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s issue, Bill McKibben reviews Charles C. Mann’s new double biography of William Vogt and Norman Bourlag. In 1948, Robert C. Cook reviewed Vogt’s “Road to Survival,” an eloquent treatise on earth’s future that Mann argues birthed modern environmentalism. Read an excerpt below.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Notes From the Book Review Archives', 'kicker': 'Our Back Pages', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-02T17:39:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34df672e-806f-5f0d-8b3f-4b5d48752e1f', 'word_count': 370, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34df672e-806f-5f0d-8b3f-4b5d48752e1f'}, {'abstract': 'Sales have risen at Christie’s, Sotheby’s and Phillips — but are they keeping up with the growth of global wealth?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/02/arts/auction-results-2017.html', 'snippet': 'Sales have risen at Christie’s, Sotheby’s and Phillips — but are they keeping up with the growth of global wealth?', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The international auction houses are feeling bullish once again.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/03/arts/07reyburn/07reyburn-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/03/arts/07reyburn/07reyburn-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '