e, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wales', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-02T17:50:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ceylan Yeginsu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ceylan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yeginsu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ce7bce6-99ec-51b1-b889-888f59e770f1', 'word_count': 637, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ce7bce6-99ec-51b1-b889-888f59e770f1'}, {'abstract': 'The best-selling author talks frankly about her writing process, her 1946 Olympia typewriter and her decidedly unglamorous writing attire.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/02/books/review/danielle-steel-fall-from-grace-best-seller.html', 'snippet': 'The best-selling author talks frankly about her writing process, her 1946 Olympia typewriter and her decidedly unglamorous writing attire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STEEL WORK: It might surprise you to learn that Danielle Steel — who has written 167 books and will publish six more in 2018 — spends between two and three years on each title. “Sometimes I just sit and stare into space and think about a book, or a twist in a book, or the kernel of an idea, and I follow the thought for a while and see where it goes, and try to envision it,” she explains. “I know when an idea is right for me when it just clicks, and I can tell in my gut it’s ‘the one.’” But she doesn’t immediately dive into a manuscript. “I make notes for a while before I start work on the outline. The notes are usually more about the characters. I need to know the characters really well before I start — who they are, how they think, how they feel, what has happened to them, how they grew up.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/books/review/0211-BKS-LIST/0211-BKS-LIST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 543, 'width': 544, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/books/review/0211-BKS-LIST/0211-BKS-LIST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 543, 'width': 544, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/books/review/0211-BKS-LIST/0211-BKS-LIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/11/books/review/0211-BKS-LIST/0211-BKS-LIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/books/review/0211-BKS-LIST/0211-BKS-LIST-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Danielle Steel: ‘I Know an Idea Is Right for Me When It Just Clicks’', 'kicker': 'Inside the List', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steel, Danielle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-02T17:55:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Jordan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, '