ine': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/8cdf5f60-37eb-570b-a86b-828c7b6a863d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/8cdf5f60-37eb-570b-a86b-828c7b6a863d'}, {'abstract': 'We dissect the public reaction to the “wardrobe malfunction” and offer Jackson the forgiveness she deserves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/02/podcasts/still-processing-were-still-here-for-janet.html', 'snippet': 'We dissect the public reaction to the “wardrobe malfunction” and offer Jackson the forgiveness she deserves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, in light of Justin Timberlake’s coming Super Bowl halftime appearance, we revisit his infamous 2004 “wardrobe malfunction” performance with Janet Jackson. We dissect the public reaction to “nipplegate,” why Jackson (and not Timberlake) took the fall and how the controversy changed the course of both artists’ careers. We consider Timberlake’s new musical direction in the context of his history of appropriating other cultures. And we offer Jackson the forgiveness she deserves, revisiting how her sexual experimentation led to some of our favorite moments in music history.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/02/magazine/-01still-processing-superbowl1/-01still-processing-superbowl1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/02/magazine/-01still-processing-superbowl1/-01still-processing-superbowl1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/02/magazine/-01still-processing-superbowl1/-01still-processing-superbowl1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'capt