implements in a talk at the Museum at Eldridge Street.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The discovery of a vintage bottle opener led the historian Richard Rabinowitz on a quest to discover its origins and how it might shed light on his family history. The clues took him to Edlund, a 90-year-old Burlington, Vt., kitchen tool company, and beyond. He’ll talk about it and discuss how audience members can follow his example when it comes to the stuff in the back of Grandma’s kitchen drawer: “The Great Kitchen Tool Mystery,” Sunday, 2 to 3:30 p.m., $14, $8 for students and those 65 and older, plus fees, Museum at Eldridge Street, 12 Eldridge Street (Division Street), 212-219-0302, eldridgestreet.org.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/dining/07burnertalk/merlin_132890843_02a02df8-a37d-43f8-b940-a3e458759330-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 517, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/07/dining/07burnertalk/merlin_132890843_02a02df8-a37d-43f8-b940-a3e458759330-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 517}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/dining/07burnertalk/merlin_132890843_02a02df8-a37d-43f8-b940-a3e458759330-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 882, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/dining/07burnertalk/merlin_132890843_02a02df8-a37d-43f8-b940-a3e458759330-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1764, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/dining/07burnertalk/07burnertalk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75,