 lobby of the Cook County Hospital. She had lived on Chicago’s West Side, within the same few blocks, since moving there as a 10-year-old from a segregated mill town in Alabama. But her West Side apartment and every belonging in it had burned in a fire. Without a fixed address, she stopped receiving the public-assistance checks that had helped stretch what she earned in a factory molding plaster figurines.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/magazine/11mag-projects1/11mag-11projects-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 756, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/11/magazine/11mag-projects1/11mag-11projects-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 756}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/magazine/11mag-projects1/11mag-11projects-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 813, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/magazine/11mag-projects1/11mag-11projects-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1625, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/magazine/11mag-projects1/11mag-11projects-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/11/magazine/11mag-projects1/11mag-11projects-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/magazine/11mag-projects1/11mag-11projects-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Towers Came Down, and With Them the Promise of Public Housing', 'kicker': 'Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After the Towers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public and Subsidized Housing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Housing and Urban Development Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demolition', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buildings (Structures)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-06T10:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97a45e68-da76-5f35-9fe1-385649dbfdc0', 'word_count': 5539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97a45e68-da76-5f35-9fe1-385649dbfdc0'}, {'abstract': 'Peggy Orenstein reviews “Buzz” and “Vibrator Nation,” two new books about the history and significance of sex toys.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/06/books/review/buzz-lieberman-vibrator-nation-comella-sex-toys.html', 'snippet': 'Peggy Orenstein reviews “Buzz” and “Vibrator Nation,” two new books about the history and significance of sex toys.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUZZ The Stimulating History of the Sex Toy By Hallie Lieberman Illustrated. 359 pp. Pegasus Books. $26.95.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/b