, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2018)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MoveOn.org', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharp, Gene', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Birmingham (Ala)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Serbia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-06T10:41:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/27029cfa-2838-5703-99b5-b5e5cd3cb47c', 'word_count': 1719, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27029cfa-2838-5703-99b5-b5e5cd3cb47c'}, {'abstract': 'As General Westmoreland’s special assistant, I had a close-up view on the Vietcong’s assault on Saigon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/06/opinion/vietnam-tet-offensive.html', 'snippet': 'As General Westmoreland’s special assistant, I had a close-up view on the Vietcong’s assault on Saigon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I arrived in Vietnam in late December 1967, I thought we might be winning the war. Gen. William Westmoreland, the American commander in Saigon, had just given a speech in Washington stating that the end was beginning “to come into view.” As a 25-year-old Army captain assigned to be Westmoreland’s special assistant, I would be handling highly classified intelligence for him, as well as sensitive privacy communications we called the “back channel.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/opinion/06Vietnam-Zengerle/merlin_133344869_3ed15830-c4df-450a-84ac-bb3a73e46be9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/07/opinion/06Vietnam-Zengerle/merlin_133344869_3ed15830-c4df-450a-84ac-bb3a73e46be9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 371}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/opinion/06Vietnam-Zengerle/merlin_133344869_3ed15830-c4df-450a-84ac-bb3a73e46be9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 633, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/opinion/06Vietnam-Zengerle/merlin_133344869_3ed15830-c4df-450a-84ac-bb3a73e46be9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1267, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/opinion/06Vietnam-Zengerle/06Vietnam-Zengerle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/07/opinion/06Vietnam-Zengerle/06Vietnam-Zengerle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/opinion/06Vietnam-Zengerle/06Vietnam-Zengerle-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What I Saw During the Tet Offensive', 'kicker': "Vietnam '67", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Westmoreland, William C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-06T10:45:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Zengerle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zengerle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6ecd2c3-f234-58c6-814d-d21af827d99e', 'word_count': 1792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6ecd2c3-f234-58c6-814d-d21af827d99e'}, {'abstract': 'The sudden drop in stock prices is a return to normal market behavior. And that could be a problem for the economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/06/opinion/stock-market-volatile.html', 'snippet': 'The sudden drop in stock prices is a return to normal market behavior. And that could be a problem for the economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fear generated by Wall Street’s sharp fall in recent days had been greatly magnified by the calm that preceded it. Before the 8 percent decline in United States stocks over the past week — which was followed by a bounce back of nearly 2 percent on Tuesday — the S. & P. 500 had gone two years without suffering a drop that large. Spoiled by this unnaturally placid stretch, many Americans had forgotten what a routine market setback even looks like.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/world/06sharma/06sha