ragraph': 'To the rest of the world, Denmark may be best known for its minimal home interiors, experimental cuisine and hygge rituals. But the small, licorice-loving country is less known as a style capital destination; when it comes to fashion, the city excels at a playful blend of bicycle-friendly comfort and Scandinavian chic. Perhaps that’s what connects the three new Danish labels Cecilie Bahnsen, Saks Potts and Rains, each of which bring a renewed energy to Copenhagen. Whereas larger Scandinavian brands dominate the market, these independent labels — which presented their new fall/winter 2018 collections at Copenhagen Fashion Week last week and have shared exclusive imagery with T — are winning over customers at home and abroad. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/06/t-magazine/06tmag-copenhagen-slide-53VJ/06tmag-copenhagen-slide-53VJ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/06/t-magazine/06tmag-copenhagen-slide-53VJ/06tmag-copenhagen-slide-53VJ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/06/t-magazine/06tmag-copenhagen-slide-53VJ/06tmag-copenhagen-slide-53VJ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/06/t-magazine/06tmag-copenhagen-slide-53VJ/06tmag-copenhagen-slide-53VJ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/06/t-magazine/06tmag-copenhagen-slide-53VJ/06tmag-copenhagen-slide-53VJ-thum