or the Olympics. They want a medal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOMAKOMAI, Japan — Yurie Adachi laughed at the photograph, as if she was revisiting an embarrassing high school yearbook portrait. The photo, taken during a practice at the 2014 Winter Olympics in Sochi, Russia, showed her on her stomach, posing with her hands on her cheeks, her skates kicking up in the air.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/sports/olympics/07oly-japan2print/merlin_133325495_de23fdb0-0b63-42be-96b6-07b3b5a4ffd3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/07/sports/olympics/07oly-japan2print/merlin_133325495_de23fdb0-0b63-42be-96b6-07b3b5a4ffd3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/sports/olympics/07oly-japan2print/merlin_133325495_de23fdb0-0b63-42be-96b6-07b3b5a4ffd3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/sports/olympics/07oly-japan2print/merlin_133325495_de23fdb0-0b63-42be-96b6-07b3b5a4ffd3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/sports/olympics/07oly-japan2print/07oly-japan1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/07/sports/olympics/07oly-japan2print/07oly-japan1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/sports/olympics/07oly-japan2print/07oly-japan1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan’s Women’s Hockey Team Wants to Be Known for Wins, Not Smiles', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A ‘Lovable Underdog’ of the Sochi Games Seeks a New Label: Medalist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2018)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-06T23:11:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Berkman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berkman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c2367db-b879-5cac-aea1-423a1aacfaeb', 'word_count': 1037, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c2367db-b879-5cac-aea1-423a1aacfaeb'}, {'abstract': 'A plan to move a key prevention program would effectively gut the embattled Office of National Drug Control Policy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/06/us/politics/ondcp-hidta-grants-justice-department.html', 'snippet': 'A plan to move a key prevention program would effectively gut the embattled Office of National Drug Control Policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — State and local law enforcement officials are fighting a Trump administration proposal to move oversight of a $275 million drug prevention program to the Justice Department, fearing that such a move would steer the country’s drug-fighting strategy toward federal legal crackdowns and away from years of holistic, community-based approaches.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/us/politics/07dc-drugs/merlin_132847046_2b1e9cd2-3535-4257-92f4-3be0474a1769-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/07/us/politics/07dc-drugs/merlin_132847046_2b1e9cd2-3535-4257-92f4-3be0474a1769-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/us/politics/07dc-drugs/merlin_132847046_2b1e9cd2-3535-4257-92f4-3be0474a1769-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/us/politics/07dc-drugs/merlin_132847046_2b1e9cd2-3535-4257-92f4-3be0474a1769-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/us/politics/07dc-drugs/07dc-drugs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/07/us/politics/07dc-drugs/07dc-drugs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/us/politics/07dc-drugs/07dc-drugs-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump Plan to Move Drug Prevention Program to Justice Dept. Prompts Protests', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Plan to Shift Federal Drug Prevention Program Faces Resistance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'White House Office of National Drug Control Policy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Aid (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of Management and Budget (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-06T23:22:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ali Watkins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ali', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Watkins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5b39c35-becd-5087-bc0c-c358451cc23e', 'word_count': 1069, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5b39c35-becd-5087-bc0c-c358451cc23e'}, {'abstract': 'Thanks to the congressional Republicans’ memo, the former Trump campaign adviser suddenly finds himself with a lot more friends on the right.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/06/magazine/the-happy-martyrdom-of-carter-page.html', 'snippet': 'Thanks to the congressional Republicans’ memo, the former Trump campaign adviser suddenly finds himself with a lot more friends on the right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday night, Carter Page was finally ready for his Fox News close-up. It had been nearly a year since he began his one-man public-relations offensive to rebut accusations that, as a Trump campaign adviser, he colluded with Russia. He had appeared numerous times on CNN, MSNBC and the networks, typically opposite their star anchors. Unlike almost everyone else caught up in the Trump-Russia scandal, Page was not only willing to submit to public questions; he would even answer them. Though he didn’t bring much clarity to his role, the appearances did make for great, albeit surreal, television. Like the time he insisted to Anderson Cooper that his conversation with the Russian ambassador during the Republican National Convention was not actually a “meeting.” “Anderson,” Page explained, “a great analogy is you and I were members of the same health club here in New York previously. And I remember walking by you, even though we didn’t know each other, and I said, ‘Hi, Anderson,’ and you said hello, and we, you know, had a nice little exchange for half a second. Now, does that to you constitute a meeting?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/06/magazine/06mag-page2/06mag-page2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/06/magazine/06mag-page2/06mag-page2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/06/magazine/06mag-page2/06mag-page2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 574, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/06/magazine/06mag-page2/06mag-page2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 917, 'width': 1635, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/06/magazine/06mag-page2/06mag-page2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 