'section_name': 'Briefing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Stanford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8efb78e-7cd6-5fd9-a3e3-2a8b9a266de4', 'word_count': 1173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8efb78e-7cd6-5fd9-a3e3-2a8b9a266de4'}, {'abstract': 'The agreement, subject to the approval of members of the Social Democratic Party, came at a steep price for the Christian Democrats: giving up the powerful Finance Ministry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/07/world/europe/angela-merkel-coalition-germany.html', 'snippet': 'The agreement, subject to the approval of members of the Social Democratic Party, came at a steep price for the Christian Democrats: giving up the powerful Finance Ministry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — After more than four months of tortuous negotiations, with her fate and Germany’s hanging in the balance, Chancellor Angela Merkel on Wednesday announced a deal for a new government.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/08/world/08Germany1/08Germany-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/08/world/08Germany1/08Germany-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/08/world/08Germany1/08Germany-sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 697, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/08/world/08Germany1/08Germany-sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1393, '