', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/992a4c0b-da54-5c92-83ff-876fbc0cba3d', 'word_count': 1266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/992a4c0b-da54-5c92-83ff-876fbc0cba3d'}, {'abstract': 'This issue is a celebration of all the different ways beauty is expressed and manifested, and all the different faces it wears.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/07/t-magazine/editor-letter.html', 'snippet': 'This issue is a celebration of all the different ways beauty is expressed and manifested, and all the different faces it wears.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here at T, we spend a good deal of time discussing people we admire: fashion designers, artists, writers, architects, chefs and performers of all kinds. Some are notable because they produce works of art that land at the exact right moment in the culture, that seem to not just speak to, but articulate, the global mood. Some are notable because they make art that has proven itself timeless, things or ideas in which every successive generation can find some echo of itself.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '102', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/30/t-magazine/30tmag-chart/30tmag-chart-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/30/t-magazine/30tmag-chart/30tmag-chart-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/30/t-magazine/30tmag-chart/30tmag-chart-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/30/t-magazine/30tmag-chart/30tmag-chart-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/30/t-magazine/30tmag-chart/30tmag-chart-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/30/t-magazine/30tmag-chart/30tmag-chart-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/30/t-magazine/30tmag-chart/30tmag-chart-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'T’s Women’s Fashion Issue: A Seat at the Table', 'kicker': 'Letter from the Editor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Seat at the Table', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chicago, Judy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kuma, Kengo (1954- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-07T19:03:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hanya Yanagihara', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yanagihara', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5399f621-24b9-5216-9530-a84c319ceab8', 'word_count': 844, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5399f621-24b9-5216-9530-a84c319ceab8'}, {'abstract': 'For our spring women’s fashion issue, we took inspiration from one of the feminist artist’s most iconic images — which takes on new meaning today.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/07/t-magazine/judy-chicago-cover.html', 'snippet': 'For our spring women’s fashion issue, we took inspiration from one of the feminist artist’s most iconic images — which takes on new meaning today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The inspiration for the cover of T’s women’s issue was a 1970 black-and-white photograph of Judy Chicago sitting in a boxing ring. She wears satin shorts and a sweatshirt printed with her name, a gloved hand on each knee. She looks ready to take a swing.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '104', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/t-magazine/07tmag-judy1/07tmag-judy1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/07/t-magazine/07tmag-judy1/07tmag-judy1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/t-magazine/07tmag-judy1/07tmag-judy1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/t-magazine/07tmag-judy1/07tmag-judy1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1277, 'width': 1915, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/t-magazine/07tmag-judy1/07tmag-judy1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/07/t-magazine/07tmag-judy1/07tmag-judy1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/t-magazine/07tmag-judy1/07tmag-judy1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thu