rtist Mounira Al Solh bears witness to the wounds of war with portraits of refugees that go beyond statistics to capture intimate stories.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/07/arts/design/art-institute-of-chicago-mounira-al-solh-lebanon.html', 'snippet': 'The artist Mounira Al Solh bears witness to the wounds of war with portraits of refugees that go beyond statistics to capture intimate stories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — When the civil war in Syria escalated in 2012, the violence forced many residents to flee to neighboring Lebanon. Mounira Al Solh, an artist, remembers seeing a wave of immigrants enter her native Beirut, only to encounter racist behavior there.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/09/arts/09mounira2/09mounira2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 821, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/09/arts/09mounira2/09mounira2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 821}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/09/arts/09mounira2/09mounira2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 748, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/09/arts/09mounira2/09mounira2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1496, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/09/arts/09mounira2/09mounira2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/09/arts/09mounira2/09mounira2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight