ief Discourse of Rebellion and Rebels, by George North: A Newly Uncovered Manuscript Source for Shakespeare's Plays (Book)", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-07T22:07:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Blanding', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blanding', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98ebb893-469b-5fe7-905f-7c3a5ce732ab', 'word_count': 1545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98ebb893-469b-5fe7-905f-7c3a5ce732ab'}, {'abstract': 'He helped lay the mathematical foundation for the startling idea that our universe is not alone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/07/obituaries/joseph-polchinski-63-leading-theorist-on-multiple-universes-dies.html', 'snippet': 'He helped lay the mathematical foundation for the startling idea that our universe is not alone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joseph Polchinski, one of the most creative physicists of his generation, whose work helped lay the mathematical foundation for the controversial proposition that our universe is only one in an almost endless assemblage that cosmologists call the “multiverse,” died on Friday at his home in Santa Barbara, Calif. He was 63.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/08/obituaries/08polchinsky1-print/08polchinsky1-print-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/08/obituaries/08polchinsky1-print/08polchinsky1-print-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/08/obituaries/08p