imes.com/2018/02/07/nyregion/diary-of-a-manhattan-beat-cop.html', 'snippet': 'Rita Mullaney met the Chelsea neighborhood and its characters in the 1990s, before gentrification. Some she busted. And some she preserved on film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rita Mullaney spent six years as a beat cop in Chelsea, and for much of the time since, she has been trying to develop a TV show about her work. In the meantime, there are the photographs she took of the characters on her beat: the regulars at the soup kitchen where she minded the line every day, the homeless people who came to trust her, the new rich and the very poor, the mentally ill and the woman whose week was not complete if she did not call the precinct with a noise complaint about her neighbor. It was the early 1990s, when New York was awash in crime, but Officer Mullaney’s duties entailed more social work than muscle.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/nyregion/11ALBUM2/11ALBUM2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 917, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/11/nyregion/11ALBUM2/11ALBUM2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 917}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/nyregion/11ALBUM2/11ALBUM2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 671, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/nyregion/11ALBUM2/11ALBUM2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1341, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/nyregion/11ALBUM2/11ALBUM2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'w