2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colbert, Stephen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Late Show with Stephen Colbert (TV Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Full Frontal With Samantha Bee (TV Program)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Last Week Tonight With John Oliver (TV Program)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kimmel, Jimmy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Daily Show with Trevor Noah (TV Program)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-08T09:49:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Giovanni Russonello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Giovanni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Russonello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4c740ee-e0e3-5a7f-9273-1d69da5957b3', 'word_count': 725, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4c740ee-e0e3-5a7f-9273-1d69da5957b3'}, {'abstract': 'The author and former Defense and State Department official is surprised there hasn’t been a nuclear apocalypse yet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/08/magazine/daniel-ellsberg-thinks-were-in-denial-about-nuclear-war.html', 'snippet': 'The author and former Defense and State Department official is surprised there hasn’t been a nuclear apocalypse yet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Your book “The Doomsday Machine” is a warning, based on your experience at the highest levels of nuclear planning at RAND in the early 1960s, that an accidental or intentional nuclear holocaust killing nearly every human alive could happen much more easily than most people realize — which is a pretty urgent message. Why did it take you nearly 60 years to write about it? It didn’t. I submitted the first third of the book to a publisher in 1975, as soon as the war ended. Her response was we would only sell 1,400 copies of this book. So I thought, “All right, that’s enough for every member of Congress and a lot of media people and academics.” And she said, “No, that means we wouldn’t publish it.” And that was reiterated a number of times in succeeding years.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '54', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/magazine/11mag-talk-promo/11mag-talk-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/11/magazine/11mag-talk-promo/11mag-talk-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/magazine/11mag-talk-promo/11mag-talk-promo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 578, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/magazine/11mag-talk-promo/11mag-talk-promo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1155, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/magazine/11mag-talk-promo/11mag-talk-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/11/magazine/11mag-talk-promo/11mag-talk-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/magazine/11mag-talk-promo/11mag-talk-promo-thumbLarge.jpg', 