les,” John Jakes’s “The Bastard” and Jean Auel’s “The Clan of the Cave Bear.” Over the next few years, like a flying ray, I pounced on copies of each.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/books/review/11Garner-sub/11GarnerLyall-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 97, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/11/books/review/11Garner-sub/11GarnerLyall-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 97}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/books/review/11Garner-sub/11GarnerLyall-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 165, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/books/review/11Garner-sub/11GarnerLyall-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 331, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/books/review/11Garner-sub/11Garner-sub-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/11/books/review/11Garner-sub/11Garner-sub-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/books/review/11Garner-sub/11Garner-sub-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Good Paperback Vibrations', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Good Paperback Vibrations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-08T10:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8ee3aa8-975a-517b-99cc-4fbc16c920f4', 'word_count': 1335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8ee3aa8-975a-517b-99cc-4fbc16c920f4'}, {'abstract': 'What should students be required to know and who should make decisions about what is included in the science curriculum?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/08/learning/should-schools-teach-about-climate-change.html', 'snippet': 'What should students be required to know and who should make decisions about what is included in the science curriculum?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Have you learned about climate change in your science classes? If so, what have you been taught about it? What have class discussions about climate change been like?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/science/07CLI-IDAHO/merlin_132035990_7761234a-ad4d-4be0-8e1a-f6cb6d1726e0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/07/science/07CLI-IDAHO/merlin_132035990_7761234a-ad4d-4be0-8e1a-f6cb6d1726e0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/07/science/07CLI-IDAHO/merlin_132035990_7761234a-ad4d-4be0-8e1a-f6cb6d1726e0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 102