line': {'original': 'By Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86af8dc3-d60e-529a-a024-c560c2d8c9f6', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86af8dc3-d60e-529a-a024-c560c2d8c9f6'}, {'abstract': 'As fashion month kicks off this week, meet the rising talents showing their collections in New York, London and Paris.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/09/t-magazine/fashion/new-designers-fashion-week-maddie-williams-feng-chen-wang.html', 'snippet': 'As fashion month kicks off this week, meet the rising talents showing their collections in New York, London and Paris.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maddie Williams, at just 22, is already making her debut at London Fashion Week this season. Fashion Scout, the international platform that nurtures and showcases young designers, invited Williams to be part of its fall/winter 2018 “Ones to Watch” runway show in London. “Currently, my brand is just me on a sewing machine in my parents’ front room,” says Williams, who recently interned with Vivienne Westwood. For inspiration, she imagined a group of goddess-like figures whose purpose is to fight the capitalist patriarchy. “I hope the feeling will be almost warrior-esque,” she told T.  Accordingly, her garments are designed to celebrate women’s bodies. “Why should women broaden their shoulders like men to feel powerful? Why not do the opposite?” she asks. Her fall/winter 2018 collection, an expansion of her graduate collection, is defined by exaggerated silhouettes and intensely textured, handcrafted textiles, which are made of mostly renewable or repurposed materials such as plastic bags. “I want my work to show that eco-fashion can still be visually exciting and push concepts and ideas beyond the fact of its sustainable ethos,” she says. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/08/t-magazine/fashion/08tmag-designers-slide-LAHG/08tmag-designers-slide-LAHG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/08/t-magazine/fashion/08tmag-designers-slide-LAHG/08tmag-designers-slide-LAHG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/08/t-magazine/fashion/08tmag-designers-slide-LAHG/08tmag-designers-slide-LAHG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/08/t-magazine/fashion/08tmag-designers-slide-LAHG/08tmag-designers-slide-LAHG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/08/t-magazine/fashion/08tmag-designers-slide-LAHG/08tmag-designers-slide-LAHG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/08/t-magazine/fashion/08tmag-designers-slide-LAHG/08tmag-designers-slide-LAHG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/08/t-magazine/fashion/08tmag-designers-slide-LAHG/08tmag-designers-slide-LAHG-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '5 New Designers to Watch This Season', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-09T18:10:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Fashion & Beauty', 'byline': {'original': 'By Angela Koh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Angela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Koh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a4df2b9-6603-5970-91d7-a38f97ece32f', 'word_count': 823, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a4df2b9-6603-5970-91d7-a38f97ece32f'}, {'abstract': 'The government immediately moved to revoke the bond of Mr. Howe, who admitted in court that he had violated the terms of his deal with prosecutors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/09/nyregion/todd-howe-key-witness-in-albany-corruption-trial-is-jailed.html', 'snippet': 'The government immediately moved to revoke the bond of Mr. Howe, who admitted in court that he had violated the terms of his deal with prosecutors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Todd R. Howe, the star prosecution witness in a sweeping corruption trial centered on Albany, was arrested on Thursday night, just hours after he admitted in court that he had violated the terms of his cooperation deal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/10/nyregion/10WITNESS/merlin_133347480_09ea6029-918d-4a18-a60b-dd59a4fafb6c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/10/nyregion/10WITNESS/merlin_133347480_09ea6029-918d-4a18-a60b-dd59a4fafb6c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jum