lin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/696fc246-9cbb-532a-9a08-1fee717a2db6', 'word_count': 649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/696fc246-9cbb-532a-9a08-1fee717a2db6'}, {'abstract': 'What two Times journalists learned from trying to quote more female experts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/09/insider/interpreter-gender-bias-women-experts.html', 'snippet': 'What two Times journalists learned from trying to quote more female experts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We all know we should make an effort to quote more female experts. Women are underrepresented in news coverage — by a ratio of three-to-one, studies consistently show — which both reflects and deepens gender biases in who gets to be considered an authority.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/insider/11-insider-interpreter/11-insider-interpreter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/11/insider/11-insider-interpreter/11-insider-interpreter-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 433}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/insider/11-insider-interpreter/11-insider-interpreter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 739, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/insider/11-insider-interpreter/11-insider-interpreter-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1477, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credi