s-1/11instagramdogs-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is Your Dog Ready for Instagram?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So You Think Your Dog Is Instagram’s Next Star', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN KENNEL CLUB', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Instagram Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-10T11:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04c49339-a1aa-566a-bb6d-8a8e1373715e', 'word_count': 1584, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04c49339-a1aa-566a-bb6d-8a8e1373715e'}, {'abstract': 'When a family experiences loss, familial roles are often redefined. In today’s episode, the Sugars answer letters from people who are unexpectedly charged with caring for their relatives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/10/podcasts/listen-to-dear-sugars-letters-from-a-pretend-stepdaughter-and-a-pretend-momma.html', 'snippet': 'When a family experiences loss, familial roles are often redefined. In today’s episode, the Sugars answer letters from people who are unexpectedly charged with caring for their relatives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After her brother died, the writer Jessie Glenn became consumed with caring for her brother’s daughter. She transferred her niece’s belongings from her brother’s house to hers and meticulously recreated her niece’s bedroom, from paint color to stuffed animal placement. When her niece wanted to talk to her dad, Ms. Glenn responded using her brother’s email address. Ms. Glenn knew she could never replace her niece’s father but she was determined to act as a proxy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/08/22/insider/SUGARS-article-art/SUGARS-article-art-articleLarge-v5.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/08/22/insider/SUGARS-article-art/SUGARS-article-art-articleLarge-v5.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 451}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/08/22/insider/SUGARS-article-art/SUGARS-article-art-jumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 957, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/08/22/insider/SUGARS-article-art/SUGARS-article-art-superJumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 957, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/08/22/insider/SUGARS-article-art/SUGARS-article-art-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/08/22/insider/SUGARS-article-art/SUGARS-article-art-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/08/22/insider/SUGARS-article-art/SUGARS-article-art-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '“Listen to ‘Dear Sugars’: Letters From a ‘Pretend Stepdaughter’ and a ‘Pretend Momma’', 'kicker': 'Dear Sugars', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Podcasts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strayed, Cheryl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-10T11:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Podcasts', 'section_name': 'Podcasts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91227eff-c035-53c6-86a6-c4f47f8d05b8', 'word_count': 438, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91227eff-c035-53c6-86a6-c4f47f8d05b8'}, {'abstract': 'Biathlon is a cross-country ski race that is interrupted periodically for the athletes to pull a rifle off their backs, point it at a target and shoot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/10/sports/olympics/biathlon-winter-olympics-rifle-gun.html', 'snippet': 'Biathlon is a cross-country ski race that is interrupted periodically for the athletes to pull a rifle off their backs, point it at a target and shoot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A decathlon has 10 events, a heptathlon has seven and a triathlon has three. The biathlon, then, has just two. And an odd couple they are: cross-country skiing and shooting.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/11/sports/10biathlon-explainer/merlin_133569537_bbbdb219-5605-4674-9cee-19dfebd2fff0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/11/sports/10biathlon-explainer/merlin_133569537_bbbdb219-5605-4674-9cee