icle', 'news_desk': 'Watching', 'section_name': 'Watching', 'byline': {'original': 'By Watching Staff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Watching', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Staff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7eef1c3-ae82-518f-b4c8-48a0a37d3ce0', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7eef1c3-ae82-518f-b4c8-48a0a37d3ce0'}, {'abstract': 'Beecher’s Handmade Cheese in the Flatiron district will host weekly wine and cheese and beer and cheese nights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/12/dining/cheese-beer-wine-beechers-handmade.html', 'snippet': 'Beecher’s Handmade Cheese in the Flatiron district will host weekly wine and cheese and beer and cheese nights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Beecher’s Handmade Cheese in the Flatiron district — the Seattle-based cheesemaker, shop and restaurant — has introduced cheese and beer pairing sessions on Monday evenings, and cheese and wine on Tuesday evenings. A variety of artisanal American cheeses are served with an array of drinks, some typical and some surprising. Toward the end, each session evolves into a cocktail party: Beer and cheese pairings, Mondays 7 to 9 p.m., $75; wine and cheese, Tuesdays 7 to 9 p.m., $85; Beecher’s Handmade Cheese, 900 Broadway (20th Street), 212-466-3340, store.beechershandmadecheese.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/14/dining/14burnercheese/merlin_132843188_89b07594-da32-45d6-b1a9-bdc94bb4d96f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/14/dining/14burnercheese/merlin_132843188_89b07594-da32-45d6-b1a9-bdc94bb4d96f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'c