be-8369-5d20-ba42-d7433f65517f'}, {'abstract': 'Walter Mosley leads off the Crime column, followed by a first novel set in rural Cornwall and series prequels from Charles Finch and Trudy Nan Boyce.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/13/books/review/new-crime-fiction-walter-mosley.html', 'snippet': 'Walter Mosley leads off the Crime column, followed by a first novel set in rural Cornwall and series prequels from Charles Finch and Trudy Nan Boyce.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They may look like soul brothers, but Joe King Oliver, a New York private eye who makes his first appearance in Walter Mosley’s new crime novel, DOWN THE RIVER UNTO THE SEA (Mulholland/Little, Brown, $27), parts company with the author’s previous detectives, Easy Rawlins and Leonid McGill. Unlike those more charismatic protagonists, King has no major sins staining his soul, and since he spent years doing hard time for a crime he didn’t commit, he has no need for redemption. While that makes this disgraced ex-cop an authentic hero, it also puts him at a disadvantage because (let’s come clean) virtuous victims just aren’t as much fun as bad boys.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/books/review/18Crime/18Crime-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 565, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/18/books/review/18Crime/18Crime-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 565}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/books/review/18Crime/18Crime-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 964, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/books/review/18Crime/18Crime-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1929, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/books/review/18Crime/18Crime-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/18/books/review/18Crime/18Crime-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/books/review/18Crime/18Crime-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fans of Easy Rawlins and Leonid McGill, Meet Joe King Oliver', 'kicker': 'Crime', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Getting His Mojo Back', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Down the River Unto the Sea (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mosley, Walter Ellis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Unforgotten (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Powell, Laura Jayne', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Woman in the Water (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Finch, Charles', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "The Policeman's Daughter (Book)", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boyce, Trudy Nan (1946- )', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-13T10:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marilyn Stasio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marilyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stasio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efe4aad8-e643-531c-8e88-35d340f71d9d', 'word_count': 867, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efe4aad8-e643-531c-8e88-35d340f71d9d'}, {'abstract': 'Love yourself a little more this week. There’s a lot of cute stuff out there. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/13/style/treat-yourself-for-valentines-day.html', 'snippet': 'Love yourself a little more this week. There’s a lot of cute stuff out there. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s impossible to know what Saint Valentine, the pious fellow for whom V-Day is named, would think of the pink glitter- and chocolate-laden holiday we celebrate this week. But given that the sentimental Victorian-era festival from which the holiday derives was based on the flimsiest of premises, there’s little reason not to think of the day as an excuse to buy something nice for yourself. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/12/fashion/12BROWSE-COMBO1/12BROWSE-COMBO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/12/fashion/12BROWSE-COMBO1/12BROWSE-COMBO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/12/fashion/12BROWSE-COMBO1/12BROWSE-COMBO1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/12/fashion/12BROWSE-COMBO1/12BROWSE-COMBO1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/12/fashion/12BROWSE-COMBO1/12BROWSE-COMBO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/12/fashion/12BROWSE-COMBO1/12BROWSE-COMBO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/12/fashion/12BROWSE-COMBO1/12BROWSE-COMBO1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Treat Yourself for Valentine’s Day', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Valentine's Day", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-13T10:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hayley Phelan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hayley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Phelan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc51a00e-9358-5c03-ad8f-4859f98d0c01', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc51a00e-9358-5c03-ad8f-4859f98d0c01'}, {'abstract': 'How a group of five activists called the Valve Turners decided to fight global warming by doing whatever it takes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/13/magazine/afraid-climate-change-prison-valve-turners-global-warming.html', 'snippet': 'How a group of five activists called the Valve Turners decided to fight global warming by doing whatever it takes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Oct. 11, 2016, Michael Foster and two companions rose before dawn, left their budget hotel in Grand Forks, N.D., and drove a white rental sedan toward the Canadian border, diligently minding the speed limit. The day was cold and overcast, and Foster, his diminutive frame wrapped in a down jacket, had prepared for a morning outdoors. As the driver, Sam Jessup, followed a succession of laser-straight farm roads through the sugar-beet fields, and a documentary filmmaker, Deia Schlosberg, recorded events from the back seat, Foster sat hunched in the passenger seat, mentally rehearsing his plan.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '42', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/magazine/18mag-valveturners1/18mag-18valveturners-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/18/magazine/18mag-valveturners1/18mag-18valveturners-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/magazine/18mag-valveturners1/18mag-18valveturners-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/magazine/18mag-valveturners1/18mag-18valveturners-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/magazine/18mag-valveturners1/18mag-18valveturners-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/18/magazine/18mag-valveturners1/18mag-18valveturners-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailh