ytimes.com/2018/02/14/t-magazine/lauren-ridloff.html', 'snippet': 'Lauren Ridloff, who was born deaf, will star onstage opposite Joshua Jackson in “Children of a Lesser God” — her first major theater acting job.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lauren Ridloff was born with long, elegant fingers, prompting her musician father and artist mother to predict she’d grow up to do something creative with her hands. This spring, Ridloff, who was also born deaf, will use them to sign onstage opposite Joshua Jackson in “Children of a Lesser God,” Mark Medoff’s 1979 play about a tumultuous romance between a deaf woman and a hearing man. That Ridloff’s first theater acting job, apart from a star turn in a Gallaudet University high school production of “The Wiz” 23 years ago (and a trial run of the show in the Berkshires last summer), will be as a Broadway lead, is a testament to her presence. “I’ve been in a room with Viola Davis and Denzel Washington, and she has that,” says director Kenny Leon.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '109', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/30/t-magazine/30tmag-ppt1/30tmag-ppt1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/30/t-magazine/30tmag-ppt1/30tmag-ppt1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/30/t-magazine/30tmag-ppt1/30tmag-ppt1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/30/t-magazine/30tmag-ppt1/30tmag-ppt1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 