ge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Leaders Reconsider Ban on Pell Grants for Prisoners', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Senators Consider Revoking a Ban on Pell Grants for Prisoners', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Aid (Education)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pell Grants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ex-Convicts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-15T10:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erica L. Green', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Green', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8170487-2f05-57bd-b885-35c8dcc29029', 'word_count': 1110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8170487-2f05-57bd-b885-35c8dcc29029'}, {'abstract': 'From upstart creative spaces and obscure bars to neighborhoods where a surprising urban tranquillity reigns, Bangkok remains ripe for discovery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/15/travel/36-hours-what-to-do-in-bangkok.html', 'snippet': 'From upstart creative spaces and obscure bars to neighborhoods where a surprising urban tranquillity reigns, Bangkok remains ripe for discovery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the first Thai words that foreigners learn in Bangkok is farang, or foreigner. And no wonder. More than 20 million farang descend on the temples and temptations of Thailand’s capital every year, making it one of the planet’s most visited cities. You run into each other in hotels and restaurants, in the air-conditioned mega-malls of Siam Square, at the teeming Chatuchak outdoor market and the Buddhist sites of Wat Pho and Wat Arun. Together, you jostle through the crowds along the buzzing Sukhumvit strip and the backpacker haven of Khao San Road. And there you are again, venturing into the famous go-go bars of Patpong and Soi Cowboy. Fortunately, Bangkok is vast and fast-evolving, with many remote corners and newly minted hangouts. From upstart creative spaces and restaurants to obscure back street bars to the under-visited Thonburi district, Bangkok remains ripe for discovery.  ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/travel/25Hours-Bangkok3/merlin_132521567_d697ea25-f6cd-4b04-8fd4-714ea7753fd2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/25/travel/25Hours-Bangkok3/merlin_132521567_d697ea25-f6cd-4b04-8fd4-714ea7753fd2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/travel/25Hours-Bangkok3/merlin_132521567_d697ea25-f6cd-4b04-8fd4-714ea7753fd2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/travel/25Hours-Bangkok3/merlin_132521567_d697ea25-f6cd-4b04-8fd4-714ea7753fd2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/travel/25Hours-Bangkok3/merlin_132521567_d697ea25-f6cd-4b04-8fd4-714ea7753fd2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'h