tion': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a24795e-ba29-5adf-8c8b-d7f3716afa7c', 'word_count': 815, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a24795e-ba29-5adf-8c8b-d7f3716afa7c'}, {'abstract': 'The government’s intelligence agencies warn of big problems ahead, despite what the president might say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/15/opinion/guide-climate-change.html', 'snippet': 'The government’s intelligence agencies warn of big problems ahead, despite what the president might say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Trump administration is seeking to withdraw the United States from the international accord reached in Paris in 2015 to fight climate change. It is trying to rescind regulations on the issue. It has even scrubbed mentions of global warming from government websites. Yet its attempt to suppress the facts has not entirely succeeded, with federal agencies continuing to issue warnings, including in a major climate report published last year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/15/opinion/15Gillis-web/merlin_133024433_c9b2534d-6f93-43d4-b428-dc8dad86b46a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/15/opinion/15Gillis-web/merlin_133024433_c9b2534d-6f93-43d4-b428-dc8dad86b46a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/15/opinion/15Gillis-web/merlin_133024433_c9b2534d-6f93-43d4-b428-dc8dad86b46a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/15/opinion/15Gillis-web/merlin_133024433_c9b2534d-6f93-43d4-b428-dc8dad86b46a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 's