'In Mark Pellington’s film, mourners get a helping hand in parting with cherished objects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/15/movies/nostalgia-review.html', 'snippet': 'In Mark Pellington’s film, mourners get a helping hand in parting with cherished objects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mark Pellington’s “Nostalgia” is the kind of heartfelt wallow that you feel like a heel for attacking. A soggy string of Hallmark moments designed to interrogate the value of the objects we cherish, the movie is front-loaded with major stars and squelching with sentiment. To say it’s depressing, then, is to state the obvious; less evident is why Mr. Pellington, previously known for suspenseful thrillers like “Arlington Road” and “The Mothman Prophecies,” would dive down this rabbit hole at all.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/16/movies/16nostalgia/merlin_133544711_81660852-19e4-4b8a-b072-200ceb83d311-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 277, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/16/movies/16nostalgia/merlin_133544711_81660852-19e4-4b8a-b072-200ceb83d311-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 277}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/16/movies/16nostalgia/merlin_133544711_81660852-19e4-4b8a-b072-200ceb83d311-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 472, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/16/movies/16nostalgia/merlin_133544711_81660852-19e4-4b8a-b072-200ceb83d311-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 1735, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'im