nstrates a New Trick', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Camouflage', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gonzalez-Bellido, Paloma', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wardill, Trevor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muscles', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'iScience (Journal)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-15T17:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Veronique Greenwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Veronique', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2376410-1972-5a8c-878a-f2907dda07e5', 'word_count': 604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2376410-1972-5a8c-878a-f2907dda07e5'}, {'abstract': 'Why European designers have fallen in love (yet again) with the romance of the American country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/15/t-magazine/fashion/southwest-style-inspiration.html', 'snippet': 'Why European designers have fallen in love (yet again) with the romance of the American country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every few years, with the regularity, if not quite the frequency, of the full-moon cycle, Southwestern style comes back in fashion. The look, which is composed of Native American, Spanish and “Anglo” influences (Spanish colonizers arrived in the American Southwest in the 1500s, and white ranchers and farmers came three centuries later), mixes cowboy boots, bolo ties, bolero hats, concho belts, Western shirts, silver and turquoise jewelry, Navajo prints, suede moccasins and fringe and leather everything. The line between cool and corny, chic and costumed, is treacherously fine.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '112', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/30/t-magazine/30tmag-ppt2/30tmag-ppt2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 523, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/30/t-magazine/30tmag-ppt2/30tmag-ppt2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 523}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/30/t-magazine/30tmag-ppt2/30tmag-ppt2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 892, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/30/t-magazine/30tmag-ppt2/30tmag-ppt2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1784, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/30/t-magazine/30tmag-ppt2/30tmag-ppt2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/30/t-magazine/30tmag-ppt2/30tmag-ppt2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/30/t-magazine/30tmag-ppt2/30tmag-ppt2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cowgirl Meets Aspen Divorcée — on the Runway', 'kicker': 'Notes on the Culture', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spirit of the West', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'va