 Theodore Roosevelt’s summer White House — now a national park — is also nearby.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/15/nyregion/go-to-oyster-bay-for-the-food-stay-for-the-history.html', 'snippet': 'The hamlet is home to a popular new restaurant. But there’s history, too: Theodore Roosevelt’s summer White House — now a national park — is also nearby.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the past few decades, Oyster Bay, on Long Island’s North Shore, has been a drowsy little hamlet. In Colonial times, it was an oystering capital, then occupied by the British during the American Revolution. But after the early 20th century, when President Theodore Roosevelt and his large brood sojourned nearby, its vitality mostly ebbed. That is, until the restaurant 2 Spring gave it a wake-up poke in January.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/nyregion/18daytrip-3/merlin_133707030_7907fa03-9510-46a8-80f9-d1bf9237264e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/18/nyregion/18daytrip-3/merlin_133707030_7907fa03-9510-46a8-80f9-d1bf9237264e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/nyregion/18daytrip-3/merlin_133707030_7907fa03-9510-46a8-80f9-d1bf9237264e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/nyregion/18daytrip-3/merlin_133707030_7907fa03-9510-46a8-80f9-d1bf9237264e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': N