 MaryEllen Elia accepted a district improvement plan she had ordered, but said it left ‘critical issues’ unaddressed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York State Education Department said Thursday that it would not take control of Hempstead School District on Long Island, which has been troubled for decades by abysmal graduation rates, crumbling school buildings, violence and corruption. The state education commissioner, MaryEllen Elia, had given the district a Feb. 2 deadline to come up with an improvement plan, and on Thursday she said she had accepted it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/16/nyregion/16HEMPSTEAD/merlin_132939749_fc515fcf-f5c0-425c-bbd9-bdce28547684-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/16/nyregion/16HEMPSTEAD/merlin_132939749_fc515fcf-f5c0-425c-bbd9-bdce28547684-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/16/nyregion/16HEMPSTEAD/merlin_132939749_fc515fcf-f5c0-425c-bbd9-bdce28547684-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/16/nyregion/16HEMPSTEAD/merlin_132939749_fc515fcf-f5c0-425c-bbd9-bdce28547684-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/16/nyregion/16HEMPSTEAD/16HEMPSTEAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/16/nyregion/16HEMPSTEAD/16HEMPSTEAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/16/nyregion/16HEMPSTEAD/16HEMPSTEAD-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'State Will Not Take Over Long-Struggling Hempstead Schools', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'State Declines to Take Over Ailing Hempstead Schools', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reading and Writing Skills (Education)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graduation Rates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYS)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elia, MaryEllen (1948- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Singer, Alan J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hempstead (NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-16T00:33:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e71b8b7b-6e7c-5ff3-9315-1d2c5ed478a2', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e71b8b7b-6e7c-5ff3-9315-1d2c5ed478a2'}, {'abstract': 'For Canada to mend its systemic inequalities, the country needs to first address its problem with racism against indigenous people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/15/opinion/colten-boushie-killing-saskatchewan.html', 'snippet': 'For Canada to mend its systemic inequalities, the country needs to first address its problem with racism against indigenous people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Friday, a jury in Battleford, Saskatchewan, found Gerald Stanley not guilty of second-degree murder. Mr. Stanley, a farmer, had killed Colten Boushie, a 22-year-old indigenous man who he believed was trying to rob him. Mr. Boushie was shot in the head while sitting in the back seat of a parked vehicle.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/16/opinion/16Scrimshaw/merlin_133953449_bd97117d-d8b3-4b5d-8115-4dced3751243-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/16/opinion/16Scrimshaw/merlin_133953449_bd97117d-d8b3-4b5d-8115-4dced3751243-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/16/opinion/16Scrimshaw/merlin_133953449_bd97117d-d8b3-4b5d-8115-4dced3751243-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/16/opinion/16Scrimshaw/merlin_133953449_bd97117d-d8b3-4b5d-8115-4dced3751243-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1800, 'width': 1800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/16/opinion/16Scrimshaw/merlin_133953449_bd97117d-d8b3-4b5d-8115-4dced3751243-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/16/opinion/16Scrimshaw/merlin_133953449_bd97117d-d8b3-4b5d-8115-4dced3751243-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbna