o wronged you,” says Charles L. Griswold, a philosophy professor at Boston University. Forgiveness means abandoning anger, and that can be long, hard work — possibly a lifetime’s worth. So before you embark, clearly identify perpetrator and transgression, and make sure the situation calls for forgiveness and not something else, like mercy.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/magazine/18mag-tip/18mag-18tip-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 625, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/18/magazine/18mag-tip/18mag-18tip-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 625}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/magazine/18mag-tip/18mag-18tip-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 983, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/magazine/18mag-tip/18mag-18tip-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1439, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/magazine/18mag-tip/18mag-18tip-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/18/magazine/18mag-tip/18mag-18tip-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/magazine/18mag-tip/18mag-18tip-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {