nce, dance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The angry art of protest is flourishing these days, and its forms are as myriad as the grievances it gives voice to: marches, rallies, occupations, boycotts, black evening wear for televised awards ceremonies. Then there is the popular retro-disco-circus protest, featuring family-friendly nudity.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/17/arts/17riotSKYBOX/merlin_133978901_421f5d37-34e5-4aba-958e-bc46fb7d383e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/17/arts/17riotSKYBOX/merlin_133978901_421f5d37-34e5-4aba-958e-bc46fb7d383e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/17/arts/17riotSKYBOX/merlin_133978901_421f5d37-34e5-4aba-958e-bc46fb7d383e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/17/arts/17riotSKYBOX/merlin_133978901_421f5d37-34e5-4aba-958e-bc46fb7d383e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/17/arts/17riotSKYBOX/17riot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/17/arts/17riotSKYBOX/17riot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/17/arts/17riotSKYBOX/17riot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Riot’ and the Art of Kitsch as Protest', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Art of Kitsch as Protest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Riot (Play)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Skirball Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Thisispopbaby (Theater Co)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Irish Arts Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jennings, Jennifer', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McMahon, Phillip', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-16T15:56:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7b626da-fce5-5f9c-8744-53181925a494', 'word_count': 680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7b626da-fce5-5f9c-8744-53181925a494'}, {'abstract': 'Listening to a new crop of podcasts, with drinks in hand, women exact revenge on the true crime genre.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/16/arts/television/the-transgressive-appeal-of-the-comedy-murder-podcast.html', 'snippet': 'Listening to a new crop of podcasts, with drinks in hand, women exact revenge on the true crime genre.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Oxygen, the television network for women, rebranded itself as a true crime channel last year, it leaned into TV’s time-tested approach: a focus on gruesome and mysterious killings, disproportionately involving white female victims and sensationalized by self-serious narrators. But Oxygen also began experimenting with a new way to cover those crimes. It started a comedy podcast, “Martinis & Murder,” in which the two hosts get tipsy on homicide-themed cocktails, audibly squirm over the gory details, make catty judgments about the suspects’ life choices and use particulars of the crimes as setups for sarcastic jokes.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/17/arts/17truecrime-image/17truecrime-image-articleLarge.gif', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/17/arts/17truecrime-image/17truecrime-image-articleLarge.gif', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/17/arts/17truecrime-image/17truecrime-image-jumbo.gif', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/17/arts/17truecrime-image/17truecrime-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/17/arts/17truecrime-image/17truecrime-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/17/arts/17truecrime-image/17truecrime-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/17/arts/17truecrime-image/17truecrime-image-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'sub