None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71ed95f3-0f7e-5c17-9a44-1eb19e246218', 'word_count': 996, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71ed95f3-0f7e-5c17-9a44-1eb19e246218'}, {'abstract': 'The special counsel’s indictment detailed how crucial Facebook and Instagram were to the Russian campaign to disrupt the presidential election.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/17/technology/indictment-russian-tech-facebook.html', 'snippet': 'The special counsel’s indictment detailed how crucial Facebook and Instagram were to the Russian campaign to disrupt the presidential election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — In 2014, Russians working for a shadowy firm called the Internet Research Agency started gathering American followers in online groups focused on issues like religion and immigration. Around mid-2015, the Russians began buying digital ads to spread their messages. A year later, they tapped their followers to help organize political rallies across the United States.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/business/18FACEBOOK1/merlin_127567715_777d954c-1ff4-4fb0-82ef-73cd1532acf9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/18/business/18FACEBOOK1/merlin_127567715_777d954c-1ff4-4fb0-82ef-73cd1532acf9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/business/18FACEBOOK1/merlin_127567715_777d954c-1ff4-4fb0-82ef-73cd1532acf9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/business/18FACEBOOK1/merlin_127567715_777d954c-1ff4-4fb0-82e