ization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00769fdb-b3a0-570c-abe9-8aeb10512811', 'word_count': 998, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00769fdb-b3a0-570c-abe9-8aeb10512811'}, {'abstract': 'America has long used cash and propaganda to try to steer the outcome of foreign votes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/17/sunday-review/russia-isnt-the-only-one-meddling-in-elections-we-do-it-too.html', 'snippet': 'America has long used cash and propaganda to try to steer the outcome of foreign votes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bags of cash delivered to a Rome hotel for favored Italian candidates. Scandalous stories leaked to foreign newspapers to swing an election in Nicaragua. Millions of pamphlets, posters and stickers printed to defeat an incumbent in Serbia.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/opinion/sunday/18shane/merlin_133993817_bae1846a-577d-46bd-ad8c-3e0ea9b32493-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/18/opinion/sunday/18shane/merlin_133993817_bae1846a-577d-46bd-ad8c-3e0ea9b32493-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/opinion/sunday/18shane/merlin_133993817_bae1846a-577d-46bd-ad8c-3e0ea9b32493-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/opinion/sunday/18shane/merlin_133993817_bae1846a-577d-46bd-ad8c-3e0ea9b32493-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/opinion/sunday/18shane/18shane-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/18/opinion/sunday/18shane/18shane-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/opinion/sunday/18shane/18shane-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia Isn’t the Only One Meddling in Elections. We Do It, Too.', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'America Meddles in Elections, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Russian Interference in 2016 US Elections and Ties to Trump Associates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberwarfare and Defense', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-17T19:30:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4d04db5-0c35-5f0d-97b4-9a0120398262', 'word_count': 1535, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4d04db5-0c35-5f0d-97b4-9a0120398262'}, {'abstract': 'Officials from the judiciary and law enforcement are teaming up to try to prevent voters from being misled, arguing that freedom of speech cannot come at the cost of a tainted election.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/17/world/americas/brazil-election-fake-news.html', 'snippet': 'Officials from the judiciary and law enforcement are teaming up to try to prevent voters from being misled, arguing that freedom of speech cannot come at the cost of a tainted election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIO DE JANEIRO — Worried that Brazilians will soon be flooded with fake news ahead of a critical presidential election, the country is setting out to crack down on organized efforts to intentionally mislead voters.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/world/americas/18brazilfakenews1/merlin_132849104_3a39a88e-7477-47c8-bd6d-761414f8e92f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/18/world/americas/18brazilfakenews1/merlin_132849104_3a39a88e-7477-47c8-bd6d-761414f8e92f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/world/americas/18brazilfakenews1/merlin_132849104_3a39a88e-7477-47c8-bd6d-761414f8e92f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/world/americas/18brazilfakenews1/merlin_132849104_3a39a88e-7477-47c8-bd6d-761414f8e92f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/world/americas/18brazilfakenews1/18brazilfakenews1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/18/world/americas/18brazilfakenews1/18brazilfakenews1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/18/world/americas/18brazilfakenews1/18brazilfakenews1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brazil Looks to Crack Down on Fake News Ahead of Bitter Election', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brazil Mounts a Campaign Against Fake News', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rumors and Misinformation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WhatsApp Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Da Silva, Luiz Inacio Lula', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bolsonaro, Jair (1955- )', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-17T19:44:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ernesto Londoño', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ernesto', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Londoño', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc5279af-5190-55b3-b524-815db31fa0f4', 'word_count': 1496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc5279af-5190-55b3-b524-815db31fa0f4'}, {'abstract': 'Its election interference didn’t aim at just the outcome — it also targeted attitudes toward our democracy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/17/opinion/russia-interference-elections-trump.html', 'snippet': 'Its election interference didn’t aim at just the outcome — it also targeted attitudes toward our democracy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a Hollywood cliché that’s been adopted by villains from the trickster god Loki in Marvel’s “The Avengers” to James Bond’s “Skyfall” nemesis Raoul Silva: They are captured, only for the heroes to realize — too late! — that being caught was part of the villain’s evil plan all along. With Friday’s release of an indictment detailing Project Lakhta — the information operations component of Russia’s efforts to interfere with the 2016 presidential election — it’s worth asking whether President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia has been reading from a similar script.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/17/opinion/17sanchezWeb/merlin_113991736_42c05ccb-78b1-4cd5-8194-a9abe69fa9cb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/17/opinion/17sanchezWeb/merlin_113991736_42c05ccb-78b1-4cd5-8194-a9abe69fa9cb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/17/opinion/17sanchezWeb/merlin_113991736_42c05ccb-78b1-4cd5-8194-a9abe69fa9cb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 