ple-ethics.html', 'snippet': 'There are so many scandals in this administration that many aren’t getting the attention they deserve.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Trump’s White House has been so scandal-plagued that controversies involving cabinet members and other high-level officials that would have been front-page news in any other administration have barely registered in the public consciousness.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/19/opinion/19mon1/19mon1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/19/opinion/19mon1/19mon1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 361}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/19/opinion/19mon1/19mon1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 617, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/19/opinion/19mon1/19mon1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1234, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/19/opinion/19mon1/19mon1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/19/opinion/19mon1/19mon1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/19/opinion/19mon1/19mon1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump’s ‘Best People’ and Their Dubious Ethics', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Trump Team’s Dubious Ethics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics and Official Misconduct', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pai, Ajit', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pruitt, Scott', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shulkin, David J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carson, Benjamin S', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-19T01:27:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/20006adc-356c-5102-b278-1a445e7c340c', 'word_count': 846, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20006adc-356c-5102-b278-1a445e7c340c'}, {'abstract': 'Abusive practices in Baltimore highlight why this is so.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/18/opinion/baltimore-police-federal-oversight.html', 'snippet': 'Abusive practices in Baltimore highlight why this is so.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Trump administration acted in bad faith last year when it suggested that cities with corrupt police departments could fix the problem without federal oversight and when it tried to derail a police reform agreement that Baltimore had negotiated with the federal government in the waning days of the Obama administration.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/19/opinion/19mon2/1