rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/19/sports/19tennis/merlin_134142681_a07b4de5-58d8-427a-a785-9d134f331fc9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/19/sports/19tennis/merlin_134142681_a07b4de5-58d8-427a-a785-9d134f331fc9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/19/sports/19tennis/merlin_134142681_a07b4de5-58d8-427a-a785-9d134f331fc9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 635, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/19/sports/19tennis/merlin_134142681_a07b4de5-58d8-427a-a785-9d134f331fc9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1269, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/19/sports/19tennis/19tennis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/19/sports/19tennis/19tennis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/19/sports/19tennis/19tennis-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Open Stays Out of the Way in Tournament’s First Year', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Its Inaugural Year, New York Open Struggles to Find Its Inner Brashness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Querrey, Sam (1987- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anderson, Kevin (1986- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harrison, Ryan (1992- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Young, Donald (1989- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-19T03:36:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74027c60-a625-5116-a4b0-7c8d6788f2f6', 'word_count': 820, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74027c60-a625-5116-a4b0-7c8d6788f2f6'}, {'abstract': 'The facilities created a culture of escapism that persisted even as the world around them changed forever.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/18/t-magazine/sanatorium-europe-history.html', 'snippet': 'The facilities created a culture of escapism that persisted even as the world around them changed forever.', 'lead_paragraph': '“SICKNESS IS THE vacation of the poor,” the early 20th-century French poet Guillaume Apollinaire once said. Around that time, European factory workers routinely left their overcrowded and soot-congested cities for the Alps, where the air was fresh, dry and unsullied by inefficient machinery. They’d return to their grueling jobs rested, rejuvenated and, so the logic went, ready to work. The sojourns were doctor-prescribed, and the sites of revival — high-altitude sanatoriums, staffed with medical workers — were often state-funded. As dramatized in Vittorio De Sica’s 1973 film “A Brief Vacation,” Clara, a Calabrian mother of three living a wretched life in industrial Milan, contracts tuberculosis and is sent to a clinic in Lombardy, where, in addition to receiving X-rays and medication, she eats lavish meals, sleeps in clean white linens, has an affair with a fellow patient, makes glamorous friends and spends inordinate amounts of time bundled up on verandas staring at snow banks. “You shouldn’t read the papers,” she overhears one fellow patient advise another. “Things are so bad, they’ll raise your fever.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '105', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/14/t-magazine/14tmag-sanatoriums-slide-ERD6/14tmag-sanatoriums-slide-ERD6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/14/t-magazine/14tmag-sanatoriums-slide-ERD6/14tmag-sanatoriums-slide-ERD6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/14/t-magazine/14tmag-sanatoriums-slide-ERD6/14tmag-sanatoriums-slide-ERD6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/14/t-magazine/14tmag-sanatoriums-slide-ERD6/14tmag-sanatoriums-slide-ERD6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1535, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/14/t-magazine/14tmag-sanatoriums-slide-ERD6/14tmag-sanatoriums-slide-ERD6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/14/t-magazine/14tmag-sanatoriums-slide-ERD6/14tmag-sanatoriums-slide-ERD6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight