s when the medicines should have had no effect.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/19/health/ovarian-cancer-immunotherapy.html', 'snippet': 'Scientists are racing to understand why immunotherapy drugs have worked for a few cancer patients when the medicines should have had no effect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No one expected the four young women to live much longer. They had an extremely rare, aggressive and fatal form of ovarian cancer. There was no standard treatment.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/20/science/00CANCER1/merlin_133655895_97f15ab1-12e5-4cde-8efe-f53e4f2ec5ce-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/20/science/00CANCER1/merlin_133655895_97f15ab1-12e5-4cde-8efe-f53e4f2ec5ce-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/20/science/00CANCER1/merlin_133655895_97f15ab1-12e5-4cde-8efe-f53e4f2ec5ce-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/20/science/00CANCER1/merlin_133655895_97f15ab1-12e5-4cde-8efe-f53e4f2ec5ce-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/20/science/00CANCER1/00CANCER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/20/science/00CANCER1/00CANCER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subty