'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07999158-45af-5f0a-9241-9998efc9c8b3', 'word_count': 1287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07999158-45af-5f0a-9241-9998efc9c8b3'}, {'abstract': 'No president has ever been so fixated on his poll results. And no president has ever had less reason to care about them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/20/magazine/do-trumps-approval-numbers-tell-us-about-him-or-about-us.html', 'snippet': 'No president has ever been so fixated on his poll results. And no president has ever had less reason to care about them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every few weeks, an email arrives from the Republican National Committee, requesting my attention to a matter of great national consequence. “Approval Poll Response: PENDING” is the subject line of the latest. “The President has asked us to reach out to some of our top supporters for a one-question poll,” it begins. “The President’s job performance has been ...” There are four possible responses: “great,” “good,” “O.K.” or “other.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/magazine/25mag-firstwords/25mag-25firstwords-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/25/magazine/25mag-firstwords/25mag-25firstwords-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/magazine/25mag-firstwords/25mag-25firstwords-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/magazine/25mag-firstwords/25mag-25firstwords-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2047, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/magazine/25mag-firstwords/25mag-25firstwords-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/25/magazine/25mag-firstwords/25mag-25firstwords-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/magazine/25mag-firstwords/25mag-25firstwords-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Do Trump’s ‘Approval’ Numbers Tell Us About Him, or About Us?', 'kicker': 'First Words', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Best Regards', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gallup Poll', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boorstin, Daniel J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-20T10:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Homans', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Homans', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1501e563-5b58-5c8f-87f1-438d9e5743a1', 'word_count': 1512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1501e563-5b58-5c8f-87f1-438d9e5743a1'}, {'abstract': 'Despite some transformative growing pains, the city may well be one of the most pleasant and livable ones in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/20/travel/chattanooga-is-changing-but-its-charms-remain.html', 'snippet': 'Despite some transformative growing pains, the city may well be one of the most pleasant and livable ones in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': '“You’ve arrived! GIG CITY: Home of the Nation’s Fastest Internet” is the rather unsexy city slogan greeting visitors upon their arrival at the tiny airport in Chattanooga, Tenn. “Gig” refers to the status that Chatt (or Cha or the Nooga, depending on whom you ask) earned in 2010 as the first municipality in the United States to offer one gigabit fiber-optic internet speed to its citizens, and 10 gigabit to businesses that will pay premium prices. That clunky claim to fame has lured many a start-up to the Innovation District in its revitalized downtown. It was also a major factor in earning the city the No. 25 spot on the 52 Places to Go in 2018 list (I’m visiting every destination this year), even if it doesn’t quite sing on a postcard. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/20/travel/25PTG-chattanooga-alpha/25PTG-chattanooga-HP-slide-YEAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/20/travel/25PTG-chattanooga-alpha/25PTG-chattanooga-HP-slide-YEAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/20/travel/25PTG-chattanooga-alpha/25PTG-chattanooga-HP-slide-YEAR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/20/travel/25PTG-chattanooga-alpha/25PTG-chattanooga-HP-slide-YEAR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {