{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbohydrates', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Journal of the American Medical Assn', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gardner, Christopher D', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-20T16:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Eat', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f45aca6c-7d2d-5e53-a049-73cb46d743df', 'word_count': 1429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f45aca6c-7d2d-5e53-a049-73cb46d743df'}, {'abstract': 'She believed we have obligations to attend to our fellow humans. How could that spirit change our politics?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/20/opinion/simone-weil-human-rights-obligations.html', 'snippet': 'She believed we have obligations to attend to our fellow humans. How could that spirit change our politics?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seventy-five years ago, the French philosopher and mystic Simone Weil joined Charles de Gaulle’s Free French movement in London. We do not know if the Catholic and conservative general, who never met Weil, knew she had left her post as a professor of philosophy in order to work on assembly lines, left her family to fight alongside anarchists in Spain and left her country to escape the anti-Semitic Vichy regime. All we do know is that de Gaulle read Weil’s plan to parachute white-uniformed nurses onto battlefields, armed only with the obligation to succor the injured and sacrifice their own lives. Setting down the paper, de Gaulle blurted: “But, she’s crazy!”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/20/opinion/20stoneWeb/20stoneWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 938, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/20/opinion/20stoneWeb/20stoneWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 938}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/20/opinion/20stoneWeb/20stoneWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 656, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/20/opinion/20stoneWeb/20stoneWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1311, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/20/opinion/20stoneWeb/20stoneWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/20/opinion/20stoneWeb/20stoneWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/20/opinion/20stoneWeb/20stoneWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What We Owe to Others: Simone Weil’s Radical Reminder', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weil, Simone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank