terial': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa373d39-1da9-5c6a-bca3-21c32154e78c', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa373d39-1da9-5c6a-bca3-21c32154e78c'}, {'abstract': 'Borekas, long, stuffed Middle Eastern pastries, are now available at Green Fig on 10th Avenue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/20/dining/bourekas-green-fig-restaurant.html', 'snippet': 'Borekas, long, stuffed Middle Eastern pastries, are now available at Green Fig on 10th Avenue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bourekas are filled Middle Eastern pastries, usually savory, and popular in Israel, Turkey and elsewhere. Often shaped as triangles, they can also be oblong. At Yotel, they’re now featured to go at the Espresso Bar and are served in the Green Fig restaurant, both on the fourth floor. Sami Boztepe, Green Fig’s new pastry chef and a native of Turkey who lived in Israel, is fashioning shatteringly flaky long bourekas. Think ministrudels filled with potato, mushroom, cheese, or spinach and cheese. Serve them as is or slice them to accompany drinks: Bourekas, $4.95 each, Green Fig, fourth floor, 570 10th Avenue (42nd Street), 646-449-7790, greenfignyc.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/21/dining/21BURNER2/21BURNER2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/21/dining/21BURNER2/21BURNER2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/21/dining/21BURNER2/21BURNER2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/21/dining/21BURNER2/21BURNER2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height