1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db97502b-c906-5036-87b3-e244230af50d', 'word_count': 719, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db97502b-c906-5036-87b3-e244230af50d'}, {'abstract': 'The borough is the latest subject of the “111 Places” series of guidebooks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/20/dining/111-places-in-queens-that-you-must-not-miss-book.html', 'snippet': 'The borough is the latest subject of the “111 Places” series of guidebooks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Queens has taken its place alongside cities like Paris, Venice, Hong Kong and San Francisco in the “111 Places” series of global travel books, crammed with insider tips. About a third of the one-page recommendations will direct you to something to eat in New York’s most ethnically diverse borough. The book reveals watering holes like the Anable Basin Sailing Bar & Grill in Long Island City, sources for Romanian charcuterie in Astoria, the story behind “Spaghetti Park” in Corona and even advice on the Malaysian hawker food menu at Curry Leaves in Flushing: “111 Places in Queens That You Must Not Miss” by Joe DiStefano (Emons, $19.90).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/21/dining/21BURNER5/21burnerbook-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 587, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/21/dining/21BURNER5/21burnerbook-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 587}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/21/dining/21BURNER5/21burnerbook-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1002, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/21/dining/21BURNER5/21burnerbook-superJumb