_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/20/nyregion/giuca-murder-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'Prosecutors said they planned to retry the defendant, John Giuca, if their appeal of his recently overturned conviction is unsuccessful.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The long, strange murder case of John Giuca — one that has already seen a two-week trial, several state appeals, a federal appeal and countless legal hearings — seems destined to return to court, as Brooklyn prosecutors said on Tuesday that they planned to retry Mr. Giuca if the recent ruling overturning his conviction is upheld.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/21/nyregion/21GUICA02/merlin_134255981_f09e42cd-4dbb-48b6-b823-8220d1a81c2a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/21/nyregion/21GUICA02/merlin_134255981_f09e42cd-4dbb-48b6-b823-8220d1a81c2a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/21/nyregion/21GUICA02/merlin_134255981_f09e42cd-4dbb-48b6-b823-8220d1a81c2a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/21/nyregion/21GUICA02/merlin_134255981_f09e42cd-4dbb-48b6-b823-8220d1a81c2a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/21/nyregion/21GUICA02/21GUICA02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/21/nyregion/21GUICA02/21GUICA02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/21/nyregion/21GUICA02/21GUICA02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Nearly 15 Years, a Brooklyn Murder Case Could Return to Court', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Nearly 15 Years, a Brooklyn Murder Case Could Return to Court', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fisher, Mark S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giuca, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chun, Danny K', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giuliano, Doreen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-20T23:11:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Feuer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feuer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8640b8c9-9f80-5d57-84bf-6394ca06b6dc', 'word_count': 679, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8640b8c9-9f80-5d57-84bf-6394ca06b6dc'}, {'abstract': 'When Rhonda Bey’s appendiceal cancer did not respond to typical treatments, her doctor turned to genomic testing. Her cancer’s DNA revealed what was driving the growth of the tumor. FoundationOne®, FoundationOne®Heme, and FoundationOne CDx™ are diagnostic tests to identify genomic mutations associated with your cancer. This information, along with other information, may be used by your physician to identify potential treatment options. But these diagnostic tests do not confer any therapeutic benefit. The tests might not identify therapies that could be of benefit to you and you might not have positive outcomes with therapies identified through these tests. The outcomes described in this video are not typical and you should not expect to experience similar results. Consult your doctor about whether diagnostic testing is appropriate for you. Treatment decisions are the responsibility of your physician. These tests are available by prescription only. FoundationOne CDx™ is a next-generation sequencing based in vitro diagnostic device for detection of substitutions, insertion and deletion alterations, and copy number alterations in 324 genes and select gene rearrangements, as well as genomic signatures including microsatellite instability (MSI) and tumor mutational burden (TMB) using DNA isolated from formalin-fixed, paraffin-embedded (FFPE) tumor tissue specimens. For the complete intended use statement, including companion diagnostic indications and warnings and limitations, please see the FoundationOne CDx Technical Information, www.foundationmedicine.com/f1cdx.', 'web_url': 'https://brandedplaylist.nytimes.com/video/t-brand/100000005753774/video-ctca-enlightened-reader-tktktk.html', 'snippet': 'When Rhonda Bey’s appendiceal cancer did not respond to typical treatments, her doctor turned to genomic testing. Her cancer’s DNA revealed what was driving the growth of the tumor. FoundationOne®, FoundationOne®Heme, and FoundationOne CDx™ are di...', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Rhonda Bey’s appendiceal cancer did not respond to typical treatments, her doctor turned to genomic testing. Her cancer’s DNA revealed what was driving the growth of the tumor. FoundationOne®, FoundationOne®Heme, and FoundationOne CDx™ are diagnostic tests to identify genomic mutations associated with your cancer. This information, along with other information, may be used by your physician to identify potential treatment options. But these diagnostic tests do not confer any therapeutic benefit. The tests might not identify therapies that could be of benefit to you and you might not have positive outcomes with therapies identified through these tests. The outcomes described in this video are not typical and you should not expect to experience similar results. Consult your doctor about whether diagnostic testing is appropriate for you. Treatment decisions are the responsibility of your physician. These tests are available by prescription only. FoundationOne CDx™ is a next-generation sequencing based in vitro diagnostic device for detection of substitutions, insertion and deletion alterations, and copy number alterations in 324 genes and select gene rearrangements, as well as genomic signatures including microsatellite instability (MSI) and tumor mutational burden (TMB) using DNA isolated from formalin-fixed, paraffin-embedded (FFPE) tumor tissue specimens. For the complete intended use statement, including companion diagnostic indications and warnings and limitations, please see the FoundationOne CDx Technical Information, www.foundationmedicine.com/f1cdx.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/20/t-brand/CTCA-Enlightened-Poster-Image-FINAL/CTCA-Enlightened-Poster-Image-FINAL-articleLarge.png', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/20/t-brand/CTCA-Enlightened-Poster-Image-FINAL/CTCA-Enlightened-Poster-Image-FINAL-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/20/t-brand/CTCA-Enlightened-Poster-Image-FINAL/CTCA-Enlightened-Poster-Image-FINAL-jumbo.png', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}},