html', 'snippet': 'The British actress was speaking at an event focused on the #MeToo movement and organized by The New York Times and the How To Academy. Here are highlights of the interview.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The British actress Minnie Driver, who recently resigned from her role as an Oxfam ambassador after revelations of sexual misconduct by staff members at the charity, said on Tuesday that the conversation around sexual assault should be based on a model similar to a truth and reconciliation commission to heal wounds and move forward.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Minnie Driver Calls for ‘Truth and Reconciliation’ Model to Combat Sexual Assault', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Driver, Minnie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oxfam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '#MeToo Movement', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Damon, Matt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weinstein, Harvey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-20T23:43:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kimiko de Freytas-Tamura', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kimiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Freytas-Tamura', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce003a1c-7c13-5ef1-bf7d-01156c61d3b5', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce003a1c-7c13-5ef1-bf7d-01156c61d3b5'}, {'abstract': 'Only raw electoral power can beat the gun lobby.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/20/opinion/get-out-of-facebook-and-into-the-nras-face.html', 'snippet': 'Only raw electoral power can beat the gun lobby.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cameron Kasky, a 17-year-old at Marjory Stoneman Douglas High School who survived last week’s mass shooting, wrote a beautiful essay for CNN.com that declared: “At the end of the day, the students at my school felt one shared experience — our politicians abandoned us by failing to keep guns out of schools. But this time, my classmates and I are going to hold them to account. This time we are going to pressure them to take action. This time we are going to force them to spend more energy protecting human lives than unborn fetuses.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/22/opinion/21friedmanWeb/merlin_134192492_51979142-9203-4e59-aeaf-8d5586a415cf-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/22/opinion/21friedmanWeb/merlin_134192492_51979142-9203-4e59-aeaf-8d5586a415cf-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/22/opinion/21friedmanWeb/merlin_134192492_51979142-9203-4e59-aeaf-8d5586a415cf-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/22/opinion/21friedmanWeb/merlin_134192492_51979142-9203-4e59-aeaf-8d5586a415cf-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1417, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image'