cker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Queen Showed Up; Optimism Was Invited', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'London Fashion Week', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elizabeth II, Queen of Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Richard (Designer)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Burberry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anderson, Jonathan William (1984- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kane, Christopher (1982- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-21T18:46:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Schneier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/339a282a-f65c-51ef-a37b-1f812690068d', 'word_count': 1642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/339a282a-f65c-51ef-a37b-1f812690068d'}, {'abstract': 'The Radiohead guitarist has been nominated for an Oscar for best original score. If he wins, he may need to thank Bach, Messiaen and Britten.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/21/arts/music/phantom-thread-jonny-greenwood-original-score-oscar.html', 'snippet': 'The Radiohead guitarist has been nominated for an Oscar for best original score. If he wins, he may need to thank Bach, Messiaen and Britten.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Set in the haute-couture world of 1950s London, Paul Thomas Anderson’s film “Phantom Thread” brings a renowned fashion designer and a young waitress into a weird codependency. The insinuating and expressive score by Jonny Greenwood — with its blend of Minimalist-like riffs, eerie harmonies, alluring melodic lines you don’t quite trust, and piercing chords that leap about aimlessly — conveys both the posh glamour of the designer’s world and his inner obsessions.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/23/arts/23phantomscore/23phantomscore-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/23/arts/23phantomscore/23phantomscore-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/23/arts/23phantomscore/23phantomscore-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/23/arts/23phantomscore/23phantomscore-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/23/arts/23phantomscore/23phantomscore-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/23/arts/23phantomscore/23phantomscore-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/23/arts/23phantomscore/23phantomscore-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Jonny Greenwood Wove the ‘Phantom Thread’ Score', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How the Score for ‘Phantom Thread’ Was Woven', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenwood, Jonny (1971- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Phantom Thread (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Radiohead (Music Group)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDERSON, PAUL THOMAS', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-21T18:49:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/adeb7bc8-c95b-54ae-8819-6ea53d165f5c', 'word_count': 1126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/adeb7bc8-c95b-54ae-8819-6ea53d165f5c'}, {'abstract': 'Evangelists, Graham said, “have to stand in the middle in order to preach to all people, right and left.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/21/opinion/billy-graham-nonpartisan-evangelical.html', 'snippet': 'Evangelists, Graham said, “have to stand in the middle in order to preach to all people, right and left.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s difficult to overstate the influence of the Rev. Billy Graham — who died at 99 in his Montreat, N.C., home on Wednesday — on American public life, and indeed the world, over the past century. It’s estimated that the globe-trotting preacher shared the Christian message with 215 million people in more than 185 countries, an effort that resulted in millions of conversions. Life magazine once listed him as one of the 100 most important Americans of the 20th century, and a Ladies’ Home Journal survey once ranked him as a top figure in “achievements in religion” — second only to God.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/22/opinion/22Merritt/22Merritt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/22/opinion/22Merritt/22Merritt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/22/opinion/22Merritt/22Merritt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/22/opinion/22Merritt/22Merritt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/22/opinion/22Merritt/22Merritt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/22/opinion/22Merritt/22Merritt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/22/opinion/22Merritt/22Merritt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Billy Graham, the Last Nonpartisan Evangelical?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Moral Majority', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graham, Billy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jesus Christ', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Richard Milhous', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-21T18:50:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Merritt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Merritt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5355f225-7848-5041-8bf4-8b7d8c57708e', 'word_count': 1194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5355f225-7848-5041-8bf4-8b7d8c57708e'}, {'abstract': 'The improviser and choreographer Jennifer Monson’s “bend the even” presents a vision of nature as wild, powerful and unexpectedly eruptive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/21/arts/dance/review-jennifer-monson-bend-the-even.html', 'snippet': 'The improviser and choreographer Jennifer Monson’s “bend the even” presents a vision of nature as wild, powerful and unexpectedly eruptive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I knew that the creative process for “bend the even,” the latest project by the improviser and choreographer Jennifer Monson, involved rehearsals on a prairie at dawn. So when the work, which opened at the Chocolate Factory on Tuesday, began in silence and dim light, I settled in for a meditative experience, a slow reveal. But the first sound came as a shock: a floor-shaking rumble that felt like the start of an earthquake.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/24/arts/dance/24monson-review/24monson-review-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/24/arts/dance/24monson-review/24monson-review-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 665}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/24/arts/dance/24monson-review/24monson-review-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/24/arts/dance/24monson-review/24monson-review-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1849, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/24/arts/dance/24monson-review/24monson-review-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/24/arts/dance/24monson-review/24monson-review-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/24/arts/dance/24monson-review/24monson-review-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: A Dance About the Dawn, but Not the Quiet Dawn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Rumble Before Dawn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chocolate Factory, The', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monson, Jennifer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parkins, Zeena', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'bend the even (Dance)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-21T18:51:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/df2931e7-34c8-5cb6-80a9-202bb4e940e2', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df2931e7-34c8-5cb6-80a9-202bb4e940e2'}, {'abstract': "You can wear all red to work, on the weekend and at a fancy event — without feeling as if you're a walking red alert. ", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/21/fashion/all-red-everything.html', 'snippet': "You can wear all red to work, on the weekend and at a fancy event — without feeling as if you're a walking red alert. ", 'lead_paragraph': 'Head-to-toe red was a major trend on the spring 2018 runways. What’s less clear is how one who is not regularly on a runway — in other words, a regular person — should attempt the look. There’s a reason stops signs are red. Yet precisely because of its alarming qualities, red can completely energize an ensemble and perhaps even your state of mind — a bonus most of us could benefit from in late winter. Here’s how to do it without feeling as if you’re a walking target.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/22/fashion/22BROWSE1-COMBO/22BROWSE1-COMBO-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', '