ization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e49eb76-0370-52e5-a362-bb9232420a88', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e49eb76-0370-52e5-a362-bb9232420a88'}, {'abstract': 'The French doll, with a necklace of gems containing tiny photographs, brought $333,500 at auction in January. It will be in the collection of the Barry Art Museum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/21/arts/design/rochard-antique-doll-barry-art-museum-theriaults.html', 'snippet': 'The French doll, with a necklace of gems containing tiny photographs, brought $333,500 at auction in January. It will be in the collection of the Barry Art Museum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Theriault’s, an auction house in Maryland, sold a 19th-century French doll created by Antoine Edmund Rochard for a record $333,500 last month. The buyer: Carolyn Barry, a doll collector who, with her husband, Richard, provided the funds to create Old Dominion University’s new Barry Art Museum, which is set to open in October. She has given 81 dolls to the museum, and in January she had set out with a purpose: to add the Rochard doll.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/22/arts/22frenchdollsub/22frenchdollsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/22/arts/22frenchdollsub/22frenchdollsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 769}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/22/arts/22frenchdollsub/22frenchdollsub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/22/arts/22frenchdollsub