s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The western is still dead, but zombie movies are anything but. The last 15 years have given us “28 Days Later” and its sequel; a remake of “Dawn of the Dead”; the parodies “Shaun of the Dead” and “Zombieland”; three genre entries from the “Night of the Living Dead” auteur George A. Romero, who has since gone to the grave himself; the TV series “The Walking Dead” and “Fear the Walking Dead”; and the zombie-adjacent “Maze Runner” movies.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/23/arts/23THECURED-1/merlin_133995263_990a89b8-405a-48ed-a4c3-76e2e9d1821a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/23/arts/23THECURED-1/merlin_133995263_990a89b8-405a-48ed-a4c3-76e2e9d1821a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 250}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/23/arts/23THECURED-1/merlin_133995263_990a89b8-405a-48ed-a4c3-76e2e9d1821a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/23/arts/23THECURED-1/merlin_133995263_990a89b8-405a-48ed-a4c3-76e2e9d1821a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 853, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/23/arts/23THECURED-1/merlin_133995263_990a89b8-405a-48ed-a4c3-76e2e9d1821a-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/23/arts/23THECURED-1/merlin_133995263_990a89b8-405a-48ed-a4c3-76e2e9d1821a-thumbStandard.