 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters to the Editor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Letters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-23T10:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d193d56-30e3-56a0-8a4f-5a32781449e8', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d193d56-30e3-56a0-8a4f-5a32781449e8'}, {'abstract': 'Gil Schwartz on his double life as a mole in the corporate world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/23/books/review/stanley-bing-gil-schwartz.html', 'snippet': 'Gil Schwartz on his double life as a mole in the corporate world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back in the days when we all worked on Wang word processors and Richard Nixon was still the worst president ever, I joined the ranks of those condemned to wear uncomfortable shoes to work every day. I was a cringing maggot back then, and it wasn’t much fun. Like, one time, right after lunch, I was told, “Go upstairs and wait for Bill.” The chairman! What could he want of me? Cramped with terror, I sat in the lobby for one, two, three hours, guts churning. Finally, at 6:45 p.m., I poked my head into his sacred executive space.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/books/review/25Schwartz-SUB01/25Schwartz-SUB01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 639, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/25/books/review/25Schwartz-SUB01/25Schwartz-SUB01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 639}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/books/review/25Schwartz-SUB01/25Schwartz-SUB01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 961, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/books/review/25Schwartz-SUB01/25Schwartz-SUB01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1922, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/books/review/25Schwartz-SUB01/25Schwartz-SUB01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/25/books/review/25Schwartz-SUB01/25Schwartz-SUB01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/books/review/25Schwartz-SUB01/25Schwartz-SUB01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stanley Bing’s Real Identity Was a Closely Guarded Secret. Until It Wasn’t.', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stanley Bing and Me', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bing, Stanley', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-23T10:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gil Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank':