': 'nyt://article/1ee2eb09-de1e-5022-a5fe-1686dc862198'}, {'abstract': 'One of the oldest cities in China proved to be one of the less expensive trips our columnist has taken in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/23/travel/xian-china-budget-affordable.html', 'snippet': 'One of the oldest cities in China proved to be one of the less expensive trips our columnist has taken in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Travelers eventually face the predicament of a destination that is utterly defined by one particular attraction — the Pyramids outside Cairo or the Taj Mahal in Agra, for example. The question is less “Should I see this attraction?” and more “How could I possibly not see this attraction?” But any lingering doubts I had about visiting the famed Terracotta Army, built by Emperor Qin Shihuang in the 3rd century B.C., soon dissipated when I entered the main excavation site. The life-size, chalky-gray warriors were meticulously detailed and demonstrated a stunning, almost overwhelming show of force — exactly, I’m sure, the impression the emperor wished to make.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/travel/25frugal-xian-1/25frugal-xian-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/25/travel/25frugal-xian-1/25frugal-xian-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/travel/25frugal-xian-1/25frugal-xian-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/travel/25frugal-xian-1/25frugal-xian-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1399, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'su