ducation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bill Mason and Sherri Rosen-Mason are credentialed white liberals, having fought for 15 years to increase the diversity of the student body at the New Hampshire boarding school where he is the headmaster and she the director of admissions. But when their college-aged son applies to Yale and is deferred — and his best friend, whose father is black, gets in — diversity suddenly becomes discrimination. Misbehavior ensues.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/arts/25GREEN1/merlin_133854255_c9b47f56-3296-4d46-98ff-08c6c9de8c7e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/25/arts/25GREEN1/merlin_133854255_c9b47f56-3296-4d46-98ff-08c6c9de8c7e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/arts/25GREEN1/merlin_133854255_c9b47f56-3296-4d46-98ff-08c6c9de8c7e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/arts/25GREEN1/merlin_133854255_c9b47f56-3296-4d46-98ff-08c6c9de8c7e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1474, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/arts/25GREEN1/25GENDERMUSICALS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/25/arts/25GREEN1/25GENDERMUSICALS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': Non