b,” President Trump said of the officer in Parkland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Trump condemned on Friday a Parkland, Fla., sheriff’s deputy who stayed outside the school he was patrolling while a shooting rampage unfolded inside last week, even as he insisted that his proposal to arm well-trained teachers would have prevented the massacre.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump Condemns Florida Officer Who Didn’t Act; Sticks by Plan to Arm Teachers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trump Vilifies Deputy Who Failed to Act During School Killings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'School Shootings and Armed Attacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parkland, Fla, Shooting (2018)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conservative Political Action Conference', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marjory Stoneman Douglas High School (Parkland, Fla)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-23T15:22:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Hirschfeld Davis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': 'Hirschfeld', 'lastname': 'Davis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d715833-fff3-5947-a25e-ef2d1e0c480f', 'word_count': 1199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d715833-fff3-5947-a25e-ef2d1e0c480f'}, {'abstract': 'Andrey Zvyagintsev, whose “Loveless” is an Oscar nominee for best foreign film, is the rare director in Russia who tackles social and political issues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/23/world/europe/andrey-zvyagintsev-russia-loveless.html', 'snippet': 'Andrey Zvyagintsev, whose “Loveless” is an Oscar nominee for best foreign film, is the rare director in Russia who tackles social and political issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — While shooting “Loveless,” an Oscar nominee this year for best foreign film, Andrey Zvyagintsev repeated virtually every scene again and again — 12 takes on average, according to his cinematographer, sometimes as many as 28.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/24/world/24RUSSIA-DIRECTOR-01/merlin_133831007_caee3401-2ccc-4112-a12d-a5da62332b4b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/24/world/24RUSSIA-DIRECTOR-01/merlin_133831007_caee3401-2ccc-4112-a12d-a5da62332b4b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/24/world/24RUSSIA-DIRECTOR-01/merlin_133831007_caee3401-2ccc-4112-a12d-a5da62332b4b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/24/world/24RUSSIA-DIRECTOR-01/merlin_133831007_caee3401-2ccc-4112-a12d-a5da62332b4b-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/24/world/24RUSSIA-DIRECTOR-01/19RUSSIA-DIRECTOR-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/24/world/24RUSSI