by the Reds, is the number he associates with his playing career.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/23/sports/baseball/aaron-boones-no-17-its-personal-not-motivational.html', 'snippet': 'Boone, the new Yankees’ manager, wore No. 19 as a Yankees player in 2003, but No. 17, given to him by the Reds, is the number he associates with his playing career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — The baseball season is an endurance test, running from mid-February until at least the end of October for two lucky teams. In a game that is played at a languid pace — no matter how many times a catcher is permitted to visit the pitcher’s mound — there are surely moments, like a midsummer weeknight game in Atlanta or Arlington, Tex., when the mind may wander.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/sports/25yankees3-print/merlin_134500962_559c91e6-b7a4-48a4-b0d1-a358fa664a51-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/25/sports/25yankees3-print/merlin_134500962_559c91e6-b7a4-48a4-b0d1-a358fa664a51-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/sports/25yankees3-print/merlin_134500962_559c91e6-b7a4-48a4-b0d1-a358fa664a51-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/sports/25yankees3-print/merlin_134500962_559c91e6-b7a4-48a4-b0d1-a358fa664a51-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/sports/25yankees3-print/merlin_134500962_559c91e6-b7a4-48a4-b0d1-a358fa664a51-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/25/sports/25yankees3-print/merlin_134500962_559c91e6-b7a4-48a4-b0d1-a358fa664a51-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/25/sports/25yankees3-print/merlin_134500962_559c91e6-b7a4-48a4-b0d1-a358fa664a51-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Aaron Boone’s No. 17? It’s Personal, Not Motivational', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Yankees’ New Manager Takes a Number, and Decides Not to Use Girardi’s', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uniforms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boone, Aaron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romine, Austin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Girardi, Joe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-24T02:51:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Billy Witz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Billy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Witz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06414628-cf8f-5b91-82c3-ab8ba15197bc', 'word_count': 1041, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06414628-cf8f-5b91-82c3-ab8ba15197bc'}, {'abstract': 'In the criminal justice system, there are difficult puzzles. This one is by John Guzzetta.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/23/crosswords/daily-puzzle-2018-02-24.html', 'snippet': 'In the criminal justice system, there are difficult puzzles. This one is by John Guzzetta.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SATURDAY PUZZLE — I was struck by two aspects of this Saturday puzzle by John Guzzetta, one very specific, one broad. First, for some reason, a pair of long crossing entries stuck out to me — PAROLE HEARING and BAILED OUT. That inspired the silly readout under the headline today, and just struck me as extra clever. It couldn’t be my own conscience, which is as innocent as a spring lamb, and certainly couldn’t be because the long, extremely slow-moving arm of the law has been on my blameless mind these days. Nevertheless, I appreciated it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/24/crosswords/24wordplay-cantilever/merlin_14404605_5867b70a-1d02-4cd6-b072-cb850eca4407-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/24/crosswords/24wordplay-cantilever/merlin_14404605_5867b70a-1d02-4cd6-b072-cb850eca4407-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/24/crosswords/24wordplay-cantilever/merlin_14404605_5867b70a-1d02-4cd6-b072-cb850eca4407-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/24/crosswords/24wordplay-cantilever/merlin_14404605_5867b70a-1d02-4cd6-b072-cb850eca4407-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': N