'article', 'news_desk': 'SpecialSections', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vanessa Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vanessa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4be04c0-bacf-589b-ab97-b82b5efa2d2b', 'word_count': 952, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4be04c0-bacf-589b-ab97-b82b5efa2d2b'}, {'abstract': 'I spoke the truth for the sake of every conservative disgusted by what has happened to our movement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/25/opinion/im-glad-i-got-booed-at-cpac.html', 'snippet': 'I spoke the truth for the sake of every conservative disgusted by what has happened to our movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve been a conservative my entire life. I fell hard for William F. Buckley as a teenager and my first job was as editorial assistant at Buckley’s National Review, followed by stints writing speeches for first lady Nancy Reagan and then working for the Gipper himself. Looking toward the 1988 race, Vice President George H.W. Bush wasn’t conservative enough for me. I went to work as a speechwriter for Representative Jack Kemp in 1986.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/26/world/25charen/25charen-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/26/world/25charen/25charen-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/26/world/25charen/25charen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/26/world/25charen/25charen-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/26/world/25charen/25charen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/26/world/25charen/25charen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/26/world/25charen/25charen-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I’m Glad I Got Booed at CPAC', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conservative Political Action Conference', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '#MeToo Movement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-25T15:15:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mona Charen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Charen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/33ace580-6708-5677-a5e4-427a29ed8bba', 'word_count': 919, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33ace580-6708-5677-a5e4-427a29ed8bba'}, {'abstract': 'Penne alla vodka, Sri Lankan-style dal or egg drop soup: Make dinner count in the days ahead.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/25/dining/what-to-cook-this-week-newsletter.html', 'snippet': 'Penne alla vodka, Sri Lankan-style dal or egg drop soup: Make dinner count in the days ahead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning! It’s extra good because the grocery store I drive out to on the weekends just got another shipment of those giant, lumpy, beautiful mandarin oranges called dekopon, or shiranuhi, and they’re sweet and juicy and seedless and $1.99 apiece. I can’t get enough of them, and I bought some extra to peel for dessert tomorrow after Nigella Lawson’s penne alla vodka, which seems like a superlative way to take the edge off a Monday night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/27/dining/27Vegetarian2-copy/27Vegitarian2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/09/27/dining/27Vegetarian2-copy/27Vegitarian2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/27/dining/27Vegetarian2-copy/27Vegitarian2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/27/dining/27Vegetarian2-copy/27Vegitarian2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/27/dining/27Vegetarian2-copy/27Vegetarian2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/09/27/dining/27Vegetarian2-copy/27Vegetarian2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/09/27/dining/27Vegetarian2-copy/27Vegetarian2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Cook This Week', 'kicker': 'What to Cook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-25T15:29:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tejal Rao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tejal', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dff22f0e-9cd5-5609-bedd-112c91fdcb23', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dff22f0e-9cd5-5609-bedd-112c91fdcb23'}, {'abstract': 'In “There Are No Dead Here,” Maria McFarland Sánchez-Moreno documents the violence carried out by paramilitary groups in Colombia, and three men who have tried to help solve the problem against enormous odds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/25/books/there-are-no-dead-here-colombia-maria-mcfarland-sanchez-moreno.html', 'snippet': 'In “There Are No Dead Here,” Maria McFarland Sánchez-Moreno documents the violence carried out by paramilitary groups in Colombia, and three men who have tried to help solve the problem against enormous odds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the drug kingpin Pablo Escobar was killed in 1993, Colombia’s bloody troubles did not die with him. In “There Are No Dead Here,” Maria McFarland Sánchez-Moreno, who spent years as a Colombia researcher for Human Rights Watch, writes about the harrowing violence carried out by paramilitary groups that bloomed in the country in the late 1990s. She focuses on the stories of three men who have tried to help solve the problem against enormous odds: the human rights activist Jesús María Valle, who was murdered for what he exposed; the prosecutor Iván Velásquez; and the journalist Ricardo Calderón. The book covers their dangerous efforts, the links between the paramilitaries and Colombia’s political establishment, and the influence of the United States Drug Enforcement Administration and its war on drugs. Ms. McFarland, now the executive director of the Drug Policy Alliance, discusses below the bravery of her subjects, the inspiration she takes from photojournalists who work in conflict areas and more.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/26/arts/26mcfarland1/26mcfarland1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 893, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/26/arts/26mcfarland1/26mcfarland1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 893}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/26/arts/26mcfarland1/26mcfarland1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 689, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/26/arts/26mcfarland1/26mcfarland1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1377, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/26/arts/26mcfarland1/26mcfarland1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/26/arts/26mcfarland1/26mcfarland1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/26/arts/26mcfarland1/26mcfarland1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tell Us 5 Things About Your Book: Fighting Terror and Corruption in Colombia', 'kicker': 'Q. & A.', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Intrepid Souls Fighting Drugs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McFarland Sanchez-Moreno, Maria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'There Are No Dead Here: A Story of Murder and Denial in Colombia (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Drug Enforcement Administration', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-25T16:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/52198cfb-e5b4-5d48-8cca-56d20d21d68f', 'word_count': 1008, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52198cfb-e5b4-5d48-8cca-56d20d21d68f'}, {'abstract': 'NBC’s suburban-crime caper is well cast and enjoyable, but it needs time to figure out how seriously it wants to take its premise.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/25/arts/television/good-girls-review-nbc-christina-hendricks.html', 'snippet': 'NBC’s suburban-crime caper is well cast and enjoyable, but it needs time to figure out how seriously it wants to take its premise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are reasons, which quickly become apparent, that “Good Girls” is not called “Breaking Bad Girls.” But the surface parallels to “Breaking Bad,” the teacher-turned-drug-dealer drama, are tough to miss.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/26/arts/26goodgirls-pix/merlin_133349141_9274a193-346b-47e4-9f05-ed0206541f99-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/26/arts/26goodgirls-pix/merlin_133349141_9274a193-346b-47e4-9f05-ed0206541f99-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/26/arts/26goodgirls-pix/merlin_133349141_9274a193-346b-47e4-9f05-ed0206541f99-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/26/arts/26goodgirls-pix/merlin_133349141_9274a193-346b-47e4-9f05-ed0206541f99-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/26/arts/26goodgirls-pix/26ugly-pix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbSta