e while promoting it abroad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/27/climate/coal-kenya-china-power.html', 'snippet': 'A project near a world heritage site in Kenya embodies a contradiction of Chinese climate leadership: Cutting coal use at home while promoting it abroad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAMU, Kenya — Across a narrow channel from this historic port town, where baobabs tower over the forest and tiny crabs skitter in and out of the mangroves, Kenya could soon get its first coal-fired power plant, courtesy of China.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/03/01/world/00cli-kenyacoal1/merlin_134419337_f99b4d6a-002a-4ef3-92f9-2ee01eaeb05f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/03/01/world/00cli-kenyacoal1/merlin_134419337_f99b4d6a-002a-4ef3-92f9-2ee01eaeb05f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/03/01/world/00cli-kenyacoal1/merlin_134419337_f99b4d6a-002a-4ef3-92f9-2ee01eaeb05f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/03/01/world/00cli-kenyacoal1/merlin_134419337_f99b4d6a-002a-4ef3-92f9-2ee01eaeb05f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/03/01/world/00cli-kenyacoal1/00cli-kenyacoal1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/03/01/world/00cli-kenyacoal1/00cli-