ne, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3def688-caea-539a-9c21-6bad8e2f65f5', 'word_count': 1066, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3def688-caea-539a-9c21-6bad8e2f65f5'}, {'abstract': 'The Making Room is an evening of work by Bebe Miller and Susan Rethorst. It’s also a website that lets us see their dance-making processes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/27/arts/dance/making-room-bebe-miller-susan-rethorst.html', 'snippet': 'The Making Room is an evening of work by Bebe Miller and Susan Rethorst. It’s also a website that lets us see their dance-making processes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They may take years to make, but works of experimental dance are usually performed just a few times. That huge temporal imbalance seems like a problem, yet if you listen to many choreographers and dancers, you get the sense that just scheduling more performances wouldn’t solve everything. These artists often imply that the process, not the product, is the most valuable part of their work — at least to them. Performances, by these lights, are more like peepholes.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/28/arts/28bebemiller-3/28bebemiller-3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/28/arts/28bebemiller-3/28bebemiller-3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/28/arts/28bebemiller-3/28bebemiller-3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/28/arts/2