isn’t selling a packaged idea about what it means to be human; she does something trickier and more honest here, merely by tracing the ordinary absurdities and agonies of one woman’s life.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/03/02/arts/02ohlucy/02ohlucy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 324, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/03/02/arts/02ohlucy/02ohlucy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 324}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/03/02/arts/02ohlucy/02ohlucy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 554, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/03/02/arts/02ohlucy/02ohlucy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1107, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/03/02/arts/02ohlucy/02ohlucy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/03/02/arts/02ohlucy/02ohlucy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/03/02/arts/02ohlucy/02ohlucy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: A Tragic Wig and the Search for Happiness in ‘Oh Lucy!’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Do Blondes (in Bad Wigs) Have More Fun?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Oh Lucy! (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hartnett, Josh', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hirayanagi, Atsuko', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Terajima, Shinobu', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-02-28T21:25:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc50d2a9-d17e-50ad-8f4d-9490ec665992', 'word_count': 768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc50d2a9-d17e-50ad-8f4d-9490ec665992'}, {'abstract': 'Enfleurage, in Greenwich Village, is the place to head for aromatherapeutic resins and olfactory tinctures. And it smells nice, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/02/28/nyregion/the-sweet-smell-of-osmanthus-absolute.html', 'snippet': 'Enfleurage, in Greenwich Village, is the place to head for aromatherapeutic resins and olfactory tinctures. And it smells nice, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jan Castro, an art critic from Brooklyn, was browsing the vials at Enfleurage on a recent Sunday. She asked Joe Richkus, the production manager of the shop, which house blend he recommended — the musky smelling “earth” or the brighter toned “water”? Mr. Richkus seemed momentarily at a loss, but Amie Castaldo, an acupuncturist who practices in Midtown Manhattan, jumped in to take Ms. Castro’s pulse and examine her tongue. Its peachy paleness disclosed “an excess of water,” according to Chinese traditional medicine. A regular customer, Ms. Castaldo clearly knew her way around the tinted bottles on the shelves. “I’d recommend you get ‘earth’ to balance it,” she suggested. And the sale was made.', 'print_s